4":2}}},"docs":{"docs":{"1":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","type":"page","content":"Let coding agents use Crest","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Browse faster"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/coding-agents"},"2":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-0","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents","content":"Let coding agents on your Mac read and act on tabs in the Spaces you choose, through the Model Context Protocol server Crest includes."},"3":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-1","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/coding-agents#turn-on-agents","content":"Turn on agents"},"4":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-2","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/coding-agents#allow-an-agent","content":"Allow an agent"},"5":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-3","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/coding-agents#see-what-agents-do","content":"See what agents do"},"6":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-4","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/coding-agents#what-agents-can-reach","content":"What agents can reach"},"7":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-5","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/coding-agents#for-agent-authors","content":"For agent authors"},"8":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-6","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/coding-agents#launchers-and-other-tools","content":"Launchers and other tools"},"9":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-7","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents","content":"On Mac, coding agents you run, such as Claude Code or Codex, can use Crest as their browser: list and open tabs, read pages, click and type, take screenshots, and read a page's console and network requests. They work in the Spaces you choose, with the sites you're already signed in to there."},"10":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-8","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents","content":"Agents are off until you turn them on."},"11":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-9","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#turn-on-agents","content":"Open **Settings > Agents**."},"12":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-10","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#turn-on-agents","content":"Turn on **Allow agents to use Crest**."},"13":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-11","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#turn-on-agents","content":"Under **Spaces**, turn on each Space agents may use."},"14":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-12","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#turn-on-agents","content":"Under **Connect an Agent**, choose **Copy Setup** for your agent, and paste it in your agent's terminal or settings."},"15":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-13","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#turn-on-agents","content":"Crest must be open while an agent works. Before an agent opens a window, Crest asks you; you can let it open windows without asking until it disconnects, except private windows, which Crest always asks about."},"16":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-14","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#turn-on-agents","content":"To start Crest without bringing it to the front, a tool can run `open -g --env CREST_BACKGROUND_LAUNCH=1 -a Crest`. Crest opens your windows behind the app you're using, and comes forward only to ask you something, such as about an agent it hasn't met."},"17":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-15","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#allow-an-agent","content":"The first time an agent uses Crest, Crest asks whether to allow it. The question names the program macOS verified by its code signature, not the name the agent gives itself. Crest remembers your answer and lists the agent under **Allowed agents**. Choose **Forget** to disconnect it; Crest asks again the next time it connects."},"18":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-16","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#allow-an-agent","content":"When the program is a general interpreter, such as node or python, allowing it covers any program it runs under the same agent name."},"19":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-17","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#see-what-agents-do","content":"Each tab an agent uses shows the agent's badge and an outline in its colour, and the page shows a bar naming the agent."},"20":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-18","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#see-what-agents-do","content":"A pointer in the agent's colour shows where it clicks, hovers, fills and scrolls."},"21":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-19","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#see-what-agents-do","content":"Choose **Stop** in that bar, or **Stop Agent in This Tab** from the badge, to keep the agent out of that tab, through any of its connections, until Crest quits or you forget the agent."},"22":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-20","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#see-what-agents-do","content":"**Settings > Agents** lists the agents connected now, with what each did lately, such as the tabs it opened and closed. Choose **Disconnect** to end one's connection."},"23":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-21","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#see-what-agents-do","content":"Choose **Stop All Agents** in the Crest menu, or in **Settings > Agents**, to disconnect every agent and keep agents out of the tabs they used until Crest quits."},"24":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-22","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#see-what-agents-do","content":"Before an agent deletes history, Crest asks you, naming the agent, the address and the Space."},"25":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-23","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#see-what-agents-do","content":"Turning agents off disconnects every agent."},"26":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-24","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#what-agents-can-reach","content":"Only the Spaces you turned on. A locked Space shows agents its name and nothing in it."},"27":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-25","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#what-agents-can-reach","content":"Never into a private window, even one an agent opened for you, and never Crest's own pages, such as Settings, a browser or extension page, or a file. An agent opens an address in a private window only when it opens a new one."},"28":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-26","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#what-agents-can-reach","content":"History only in the Spaces you turned on, never private history."},"29":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-27","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#what-agents-can-reach","content":"Only `http` and `https` pages, and blank ones."},"30":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-28","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#what-agents-can-reach","content":"Not your saved passwords. A password field's value is left out of what agents read, cookies and sign-in headers are hidden in the requests they read, and request and response bodies are never shown."},"31":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-29","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#what-agents-can-reach","content":"Scripts in a page's own world only when you turn on **Let agents run scripts in pages**. A script runs with the page's own access, so it can read anything the page holds, including a password filled in on it."},"32":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-30","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#what-agents-can-reach","content":"Any program that runs as you on your Mac can run an agent you allowed. Crest's question tells agents apart so you can see and control them; it is not a defense against harmful software already on your Mac. Allow only agents you trust, and turn agents off when you don't need them."},"33":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-31","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#for-agent-authors","content":"Crest includes a Model Context Protocol server as a helper inside the app, which an agent runs over its standard input and output:"},"34":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-32","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#for-agent-authors","content":"It speaks protocol version 2026-07-28 and the earlier versions that open with `initialize`. Call `identify` first with your name and brand colour as `#RRGGBB`, so the person sees which tabs you use. Then use `list_spaces` and `list_tabs`, and read pages with `take_snapshot`, whose element `uid`s `click`, `hover`, `fill` and `scroll` take. The other tools are `open_tab`, `navigate`, `show_tab`, `close_tab`, `screenshot`, `type_text`, `press_key`, `wait_for`, `list_console_messages`, `list_network_requests`, `get_network_request`, `evaluate_script`, `read_page_text`, `handle_dialog`, `search_history`, `delete_history`, `list_search_providers`, `open_window`, `open_blank_window`, `open_quick_window` and `open_private_window`."},"35":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-33","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#for-agent-authors","content":"`read_page_text` answers a page's readable text as Markdown, without any form field's value. `handle_dialog` answers a page's alert, confirm or prompt, but never a question about leaving the page. `wait_for` also takes `url`, to wait until the tab's address contains it. Tools that open a window wait while Crest asks the person."},"36":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-34","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#for-agent-authors","content":"When a page runs on WebKit, input reaches it as script events, which some pages ignore, and its network requests show their address, type and timing without their method, status or headers."},"37":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-35","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#launchers-and-other-tools","content":"Launchers and other local tools use the same helper, approval and Spaces as coding agents."},"38":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-36","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#launchers-and-other-tools","content":"`list_spaces` says which Space is active and includes each unlocked Space's artwork. `list_tabs` says whether each tab is pinned or saved and which folders hold it."},"39":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-37","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#launchers-and-other-tools","content":"`show_tab` shows the tab itself, opening a normal window over its Space only when none is open. `close_tab` closes only open tabs."},"40":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-38","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#launchers-and-other-tools","content":"`search_history` searches the history of the allowed, unlocked Spaces, newest first. Every word of `query` must appear in the title or address, `domain` matches a host and its subdomains, and `limit` takes 1 through 1000, 25 by default."},"41":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-39","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#launchers-and-other-tools","content":"`delete_history` removes every visit to one `url`, without its fragment, from one allowed, unlocked `space`, once the person agrees. An address with no visits removes nothing and asks nothing."},"42":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-40","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#launchers-and-other-tools","content":"`list_search_providers` lists the enabled search providers and a Space's default."},"43":{"id":"/guides/coding-agents-41","page_id":"/guides/coding-agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/coding-agents#launchers-and-other-tools","content":"`open_window`, `open_blank_window` and `open_quick_window` open a window over an allowed, unlocked Space, at an `http` or `https` address where they take one. `open_private_window` answers only with the window's ID; an address opens only in a new Private Window."},"44":{"id":"/guides/command-palette","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","type":"page","content":"Use the command palette","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Browse faster"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/command-palette"},"45":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-0","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/command-palette","content":"Search, navigate, switch tabs, revisit history, search any site or ask an AI assistant, and run Crest commands from one field."},"46":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-1","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/command-palette#read-the-results","content":"Read the results"},"47":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-2","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/command-palette#complete-addresses","content":"Complete addresses"},"48":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-3","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/command-palette#search-a-site-or-ask-an-assistant","content":"Search a site or ask an assistant"},"49":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-4","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/command-palette#narrow-to-one-kind-of-result","content":"Narrow to one kind of result"},"50":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-5","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/command-palette#run-commands-by-name","content":"Run commands by name"},"51":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-6","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/command-palette#keyboard","content":"Keyboard"},"52":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-7","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/command-palette#what-the-palette-remembers","content":"What the palette remembers"},"53":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-8","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/command-palette","content":"Click the address display or press **Command-L**. The same palette can resolve a web address, search query, open tab, saved page, history entry, Space, settings page, or Crest command."},"54":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-9","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/command-palette#read-the-results","content":"The first row is what **Return** does. When one result clearly fits what you typed, it leads as the Top Hit: the address the field is completing, a tab or page you use often whose title or address starts with your text, or the result you chose before for the same text. Otherwise the first row opens the address you typed or searches for it with the Space's search engine, and it always follows a Top Hit."},"55":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-10","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/command-palette#read-the-results","content":"Below it, the palette lists tabs, pinned and saved tabs, history, actions, and other Spaces from the current Space under their own headers, then search suggestions last. Pages you visit often and recently, and open tabs you used recently, rank higher. A page that is open shows once, as its tab. Set the order, how many results each section shows, and whether results blend into one list in **Settings → Search**."},"56":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-11","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/command-palette#read-the-results","content":"Before you type, the palette shows **Recent Tabs**, the tabs you used most recently, and a few actions, in the order you set in **Settings → Search**. With Recent Tabs first, **Return** goes straight back to the tab you were on before."},"57":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-12","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/command-palette#complete-addresses","content":"As you type the start of a site you've typed or opened before, or one a tab shows, the palette fills in the rest of its address in gray. It completes the site name, without `www.`, and once you type a `/`, the next part of the path. **Return** opens what the field shows. Press **Tab**, **Right Arrow**, or **End** to accept the completion and keep typing, or **Escape** or **Delete** to reject it, which makes **Return** run what you typed."},"58":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-13","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/command-palette#search-a-site-or-ask-an-assistant","content":"Type a provider's shortcut, such as **g** for Google, **ddg** for DuckDuckGo, **yt** for YouTube, **w** for Wikipedia, or **claude**, and press **Tab**; this needs **Tab to search providers**, which is on unless you turn it off. While you type the first word, every provider it names or starts to name shows as a chip under the field, with its shortcut; the first is the one **Tab** chooses, and you can click any of them. Once a provider is chosen, a chip with its icon and color appears beside the field. Type your search and press **Return** to search that provider, or to ask an AI assistant. When what you typed is exactly a shortcut, **Tab** chooses the provider even while the field completes an address. Type `$` before a shortcut, such as `$yt`, and a space to choose the provider without pressing **Tab**. **Space to search providers** in **Settings → Search** turns this off, or lets a shortcut alone, such as `yt`, and a space choose the provider too. Its suggestions, where it offers them, come only from that provider. Press **Escape**, **Delete** in an empty field, or the chip's close control to leave and keep your text."},"59":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-14","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/command-palette#search-a-site-or-ask-an-assistant","content":"Crest offers search engines such as Google, DuckDuckGo, Bing, Brave Search and Startpage; AI assistants such as ChatGPT, Claude and Perplexity; and websites such as YouTube, Wikipedia, GitHub, Reddit and Amazon. Turn providers on or off, change their shortcuts, set their options, choose your default search and the one private windows use, and add your own in **Settings → Search**. Search providers stay on this device."},"60":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-15","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/command-palette#narrow-to-one-kind-of-result","content":"Type `@tabs`, `@history`, `@saved`, `@actions`, or `@spaces` and press **Space** or **Tab** to list every match of that kind and nothing else. Leave the same way you leave a provider. Turn these off with **@ Filters** in **Settings → Search**."},"61":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-16","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/command-palette#run-commands-by-name","content":"Type a verb or feature name such as \"archive,\" \"downloads,\" \"reader,\" \"split,\" or \"copy Markdown.\" Initials work too, such as \"tsv\" for Toggle Split View. The palette uses the same command catalog as the Mac menus and shortcut settings, so an action stays discoverable even when it has no key equivalent. Settings pages appear the same way."},"62":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-17","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/command-palette#run-commands-by-name","content":"Type arithmetic such as `24 * 7` to see the answer; **Return** copies it."},"63":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-18","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/command-palette#keyboard","content":"**Up** and **Down** arrows, or **Control-N** and **Control-P**, move the selection; **Option-Up** and **Option-Down** jump between sections."},"64":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-19","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/command-palette#keyboard","content":"**Tab** chooses the provider whose shortcut you typed, accepts a completion, or moves to the next result. **Shift-Tab** moves back."},"65":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-20","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/command-palette#keyboard","content":"**Return** runs the selected result. Hold **Command** to open it in a background tab, **Shift-Command** for a new tab, **Shift** for Split View, or **Option** for a Quick Window; the selected row shows where it will open while you hold the keys."},"66":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-21","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/command-palette#keyboard","content":"**Shift-Delete** on a history result removes it from history, and on a result the palette learned, forgets it."},"67":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-22","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/command-palette#keyboard","content":"**Escape** leaves a provider or scope, then rejects a completion, then closes the palette."},"68":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-23","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/command-palette#what-the-palette-remembers","content":"The palette learns which result you choose for what you type, so the result you usually pick for \"gi\" leads next time. It remembers this for each Space on this device only, never syncs it, and never learns in a private window. Clearing a Space's history forgets it too, and **Settings → Search → Clear Learned Choices** forgets everything it learned."},"69":{"id":"/guides/command-palette-24","page_id":"/guides/command-palette","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/command-palette#what-the-palette-remembers","content":"Search suggestions from your search engine are optional, never fetched in a private window, and separate from the tabs, history, and actions the palette finds on your device."},"70":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","type":"page","content":"Gestures and pointer actions","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Browse faster"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer"},"71":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-0","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","content":"Learn Crest’s swipes, drags, middle-click actions, context menus, and other less-obvious interactions."},"72":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-1","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#iphone","content":"iPhone"},"73":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-2","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#mac-and-ipad","content":"Mac and iPad"},"74":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-3","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#mouse-and-trackpad-details-on-mac","content":"Mouse and trackpad details on Mac"},"75":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-4","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#dragging-without-losing-work","content":"Dragging without losing work"},"76":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-5","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","content":"Many Crest actions stay out of the permanent chrome. This is the practical map for touch, trackpad, mouse, and drag and drop."},"77":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-6","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#iphone","content":"Swipe vertically on the address capsule to move between the page and tab viewer."},"78":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-7","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#iphone","content":"Swipe horizontally on the compact toolbar to page between cards in Split View. Outside a split, this gesture intentionally does nothing."},"79":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-8","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#iphone","content":"Swipe from the sidebar’s chosen edge to reveal it. Set a left- or right-side sidebar in **Settings → Appearance**."},"80":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-9","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#iphone","content":"Swipe or scroll the Space picker to move between Spaces."},"81":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-10","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#iphone","content":"Touch and hold tabs, folders, links, and Space controls for context actions."},"82":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-11","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#mac-and-ipad","content":"Drag a Split View divider to resize its columns."},"83":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-12","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#mac-and-ipad","content":"Drag a sidebar tab onto the page to create or extend a Split View."},"84":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-13","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#mac-and-ipad","content":"Drag tabs and folders to reorder them, save them in folders, or move them when a destination is shown."},"85":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-14","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#mac-and-ipad","content":"Swipe or scroll over the Space picker to change Spaces."},"86":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-15","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#mac-and-ipad","content":"Use the normal two-finger Back and Forward gesture inside web content; the page's engine owns the page-navigation gesture."},"87":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-16","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#mouse-and-trackpad-details-on-mac","content":"Right-click a tab, folder, Space, or link for its contextual actions."},"88":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-17","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#mouse-and-trackpad-details-on-mac","content":"Command-click tabs and folders to select several items; Shift-click to select a range."},"89":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-18","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#mouse-and-trackpad-details-on-mac","content":"Drag a webpage link to pull out a live Peek. **Settings → Links → Drag links to Peek** controls this gesture; hold Option to use the opposite behavior."},"90":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-19","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#mouse-and-trackpad-details-on-mac","content":"Middle-click a current tab to close it."},"91":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-20","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#mouse-and-trackpad-details-on-mac","content":"Middle-click a pinned or saved item to unload its live page while keeping the durable item."},"92":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-21","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#mouse-and-trackpad-details-on-mac","content":"Double-click the saved-location indicator on a saved tab, or its pinned tile when applicable, to return to the saved home URL."},"93":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-22","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#mouse-and-trackpad-details-on-mac","content":"Turn on **Focus follows pointer** in **Settings → Tabs** if moving the pointer between Split View cards should move focus too."},"94":{"id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer-23","page_id":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/gestures-and-pointer#dragging-without-losing-work","content":"Drag into a Saved folder to keep a page, or into a Current Tabs folder to group ongoing work. A tab moved to another Space loads under that destination profile; a tab dropped onto a page joins its Split View. Watch the insertion target before releasing when folders are nested."},"95":{"id":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts","page_id":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts","type":"page","content":"Keyboard shortcuts","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Browse faster"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts"},"96":{"id":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts-0","page_id":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts","content":"Reference every default Crest browser shortcut and customize the complete Mac command map."},"97":{"id":"/guides/keyboard-shor