rd-shortcuts#browser-surfaces-and-developer-tools","content":"| Action         | Default         |\n| -------------- | --------------- |\n| Show Downloads | Shift-Command-J |","table":"table-4"},"158":{"id":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts-62","page_id":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts#browser-surfaces-and-developer-tools","content":"| Action             | Default          |\n| ------------------ | ---------------- |\n| Show Web Inspector | Option-Command-I |","table":"table-4"},"159":{"id":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts-63","page_id":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts#browser-surfaces-and-developer-tools","content":"| Action                               | Default         |\n| ------------------------------------ | --------------- |\n| Show or Hide Developer Toolbar (Mac) | Shift-Command-I |","table":"table-4"},"160":{"id":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts-64","page_id":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts#ipad-hardware-keyboards","content":"iPad uses Crest’s shipped defaults for the commands available on that platform. Hold the Command key to inspect commands exposed by the current menu context. Full shortcut rebinding is a Mac feature."},"161":{"id":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts-65","page_id":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts#ipad-hardware-keyboards","content":"On iPad, **Option-Command-N** remains New Quick Window. New Blank Window is a Mac command."},"162":{"id":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts-66","page_id":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts#context-only-keys","content":"Some temporary interfaces have their own local actions. In Peek, **Command-W** closes the preview and **Command-O** promotes it to a full tab. **Escape** dismisses transient panels such as the command palette or Quick Window flow when dismissal is available."},"163":{"id":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts-67","page_id":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/keyboard-shortcuts#resolve-a-conflict-on-mac","content":"Search for either command in **Settings → Shortcuts**, select the row, and record a different key combination. Crest shows collisions before the replacement becomes part of your command map. Clearing a shortcut makes the action unassigned; resetting restores the shipped default."},"164":{"id":"/guides/link-routing","page_id":"/guides/link-routing","type":"page","content":"Route links to the right Space","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Browse faster"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/link-routing"},"165":{"id":"/guides/link-routing-0","page_id":"/guides/link-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/link-routing","content":"Build Air Traffic Control-style URL rules that send external links to a chosen Crest Space."},"166":{"id":"/guides/link-routing-1","page_id":"/guides/link-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/link-routing#create-a-route","content":"Create a route"},"167":{"id":"/guides/link-routing-2","page_id":"/guides/link-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/link-routing#match-deliberately","content":"Match deliberately"},"168":{"id":"/guides/link-routing-3","page_id":"/guides/link-routing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/link-routing#relationship-to-quick-window","content":"Relationship to Quick Window"},"169":{"id":"/guides/link-routing-4","page_id":"/guides/link-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/link-routing","content":"Link Routing is Crest’s equivalent of Arc’s Air Traffic Control: matching links opened from other apps can go to a specific Space before the normal external-link destination is considered."},"170":{"id":"/guides/link-routing-5","page_id":"/guides/link-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/link-routing#create-a-route","content":"Open **Settings → Links**."},"171":{"id":"/guides/link-routing-6","page_id":"/guides/link-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/link-routing#create-a-route","content":"In **Routing**, choose **New Route**."},"172":{"id":"/guides/link-routing-7","page_id":"/guides/link-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/link-routing#create-a-route","content":"Enter a URL pattern."},"173":{"id":"/guides/link-routing-8","page_id":"/guides/link-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/link-routing#create-a-route","content":"Choose **Contains** or **Exact**."},"174":{"id":"/guides/link-routing-9","page_id":"/guides/link-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/link-routing#create-a-route","content":"Choose the destination Space."},"175":{"id":"/guides/link-routing-10","page_id":"/guides/link-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/link-routing#create-a-route","content":"Routes are evaluated from top to bottom. Reorder them when a narrow rule should win before a broad one."},"176":{"id":"/guides/link-routing-11","page_id":"/guides/link-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/link-routing#match-deliberately","content":"**Exact** is best for one complete address that should always land in one Space."},"177":{"id":"/guides/link-routing-12","page_id":"/guides/link-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/link-routing#match-deliberately","content":"**Contains** is useful for a domain or stable path fragment, but a pattern that is too broad may catch unrelated links."},"178":{"id":"/guides/link-routing-13","page_id":"/guides/link-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/link-routing#match-deliberately","content":"Start with the smallest meaningful domain or URL fragment, test a link from another app, then broaden only if needed."},"179":{"id":"/guides/link-routing-14","page_id":"/guides/link-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/link-routing#relationship-to-quick-window","content":"Routing runs before the default **Links from other apps** choice. If no rule matches, Crest uses Quick Window, Most Recent Space, or the Chosen Space according to that default."},"180":{"id":"/guides/link-routing-15","page_id":"/guides/link-routing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/link-routing#relationship-to-quick-window","content":"A route targeting a protected Private Space is hidden until that Space is unlocked. This prevents its URL patterns and destination identity from leaking through Settings."},"181":{"id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","page_id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","type":"page","content":"Localhost and developer tools","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Browse faster"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools"},"182":{"id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools-0","page_id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","content":"Preview phone, desktop, and custom viewport sizes, capture pages, and inspect websites with Crest’s Mac developer tools."},"183":{"id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools-1","page_id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools#preview-a-different-viewport","content":"Preview a different viewport"},"184":{"id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools-2","page_id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools#toolbar-controls","content":"Toolbar controls"},"185":{"id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools-3","page_id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools#open-the-inspector-directly","content":"Open the inspector directly"},"186":{"id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools-4","page_id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools#security-boundary","content":"Security boundary"},"187":{"id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools-5","page_id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","content":"On Mac, Crest automatically shows its developer toolbar for local development addresses. This includes `localhost`, loopback and private-network addresses, single-label hosts, common local suffixes such as `.local` and `.test`, and file URLs."},"188":{"id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools-6","page_id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","content":"Use **Shift-Command-I** to show or hide the toolbar on any website. To stop the toolbar opening by itself on local addresses, turn off **Developer toolbar on local pages** in **Settings > General**. The shortcut still shows it whenever you want it."},"189":{"id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools-7","page_id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools#preview-a-different-viewport","content":"Choose a phone or desktop preset, or enter a custom size, in the developer toolbar. The live page renders within that viewport so you can review responsive layouts without resizing your whole browser window. Return to the normal viewport when finished."},"190":{"id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools-8","page_id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools#preview-a-different-viewport","content":"This previews the page’s layout at the chosen dimensions; it does not reproduce another device’s hardware or browser engine."},"191":{"id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools-9","page_id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools#toolbar-controls","content":"Edit the complete development URL without losing the visible route."},"192":{"id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools-10","page_id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools#toolbar-controls","content":"Copy the current link."},"193":{"id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools-11","page_id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools#toolbar-controls","content":"Open Site Settings and inspect permissions."},"194":{"id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools-12","page_id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools#toolbar-controls","content":"Use **Capture in Portrait Mode**, **Copy Full Page Capture**, or drag a region to copy it."},"195":{"id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools-13","page_id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools#toolbar-controls","content":"Toggle the inspector's Console, Network panel, or element inspection."},"196":{"id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools-14","page_id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools#toolbar-controls","content":"Automatic localhost tools follow the focused address. The manual toolbar toggle lets you inspect other sites too."},"197":{"id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools-15","page_id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools#open-the-inspector-directly","content":"Use **Option-Command-I**, the menu, or the command palette; the same shortcut closes it again. A Chromium page opens Chromium DevTools in the window, and a WebKit page opens Web Inspector. The inspector follows the focused page, including the focused card inside Split View."},"198":{"id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools-16","page_id":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/localhost-developer-tools#security-boundary","content":"Developer tools make page internals visible and can change runtime state. Use them only for sites and code you trust. A certificate warning, external-app request, or protected permission remains subject to Crest’s normal navigation and site-permission policies; localhost mode does not bypass those checks."},"199":{"id":"/guides/page-tools","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","type":"page","content":"Translate, read, and use page tools","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Browse faster"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/page-tools"},"200":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-0","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools","content":"Translate webpages on device, use Reader, find text, adjust zoom, share, and export pages."},"201":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-1","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/page-tools#translate-a-page","content":"Translate a page"},"202":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-2","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/page-tools#read-and-search","content":"Read and search"},"203":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-3","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/page-tools#video-and-audio","content":"Video and audio"},"204":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-4","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/page-tools#copy-and-share","content":"Copy and share"},"205":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-5","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/page-tools#export","content":"Export"},"206":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-6","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/page-tools#reload-choices","content":"Reload choices"},"207":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-7","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/page-tools#content-and-site-controls","content":"Content and site controls"},"208":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-8","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools","content":"Page actions operate on the focused page. In Split View, click or tap a card first so the intended page owns the command."},"209":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-9","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools","content":"On Mac, each page runs in Chromium or WebKit. Crest on iPhone and iPad uses WebKit. A few page tools depend on the page's engine, and this page notes where. To switch a page, see Chromium and WebKit on Mac."},"210":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-10","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools#translate-a-page","content":"Translate webpages on device using Apple’s Translation framework. Whole-page translation works on iPhone, iPad, and Mac, where it works on both Chromium and WebKit pages. On a Chromium page you can also select text and translate the selection from the page's context menu; it uses the same on-device translation."},"211":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-11","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools#translate-a-page","content":"On Mac, open the translation toolbar with **Shift-Command-L**. On iPhone and iPad, tap the address bar’s translation button for options, or touch and hold it to translate immediately."},"212":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-12","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools#translate-a-page","content":"Choose **Detect Language** or a source language, pick a target language, then translate. **Show Original** restores the page’s original text. Language availability depends on Apple’s support; Apple asks before downloading a language that is needed."},"213":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-13","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools#translate-a-page","content":"**Automatically Translate** is off by default. When enabled, Crest uses your preferred device language and languages already downloaded. Showing the original keeps that page untranslated until you navigate or reload."},"214":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-14","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools#translate-a-page","content":"Downloaded language packs are shared with other apps and remain on the device after Private Browsing ends."},"215":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-15","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools#read-and-search","content":"**Reader** converts a supported article into a focused reading surface. Use the page controls, menu, command palette, or assign a shortcut. Reader works on WebKit pages. On Mac, open a Chromium page in WebKit to read it in Reader."},"216":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-16","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools#read-and-search","content":"**Find in Page** uses **Command-F**. Step through matches and close Find when finished. On a Chromium page, Find shows how many matches there are and which one is selected; on a WebKit page, it shows whether there is a match."},"217":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-17","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools#read-and-search","content":"**Zoom In**, **Zoom Out**, and **Actual Size** use **Command-+**, **Command--**, and **Command-0**."},"218":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-18","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools#read-and-search","content":"Set a default zoom for pages in **Settings → Appearance**, from **50% to 300%**."},"219":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-19","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools#video-and-audio","content":"Use the sidebar’s Now Playing controls for eligible active media. On Mac, supported videos can open in **Picture in Picture**. Turn on **Picture in Picture when switching tabs** in **Settings → General** to start it automatically. Availability depends on the website and its player."},"220":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-20","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools#copy-and-share","content":"**Copy Page Link** uses **Shift-Command-C**."},"221":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-21","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools#copy-and-share","content":"**Copy Page Link as Markdown** uses **Option-Shift-Command-C** and produces a title-and-URL link suitable for notes or issue trackers."},"222":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-22","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools#copy-and-share","content":"**Share Page** opens the platform share sheet when available."},"223":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-23","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools#export","content":"**Print Page** uses **Command-P**."},"224":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-24","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools#export","content":"**Export as PDF** writes a portable rendered document."},"225":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-25","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools#export","content":"**Save Web Archive** saves the whole page in one file. A Chromium page saves an `.mhtml` file, and a WebKit page saves a `.webarchive` file."},"226":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-26","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools#export","content":"**File → Open File…** offers the archive format of the focused page's engine. Chromium cannot open a `.webarchive`, and WebKit cannot open an `.mhtml` file."},"227":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-27","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools#export","content":"Export and Share are available through menus and the command palette even when no default shortcut is assigned."},"228":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-28","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools#reload-choices","content":"**Command-R** performs a normal reload. **Shift-Command-R** reloads from the origin when a cached response is not what you need. **Command-.** stops the current load."},"229":{"id":"/guides/page-tools-29","page_id":"/guides/page-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/page-tools#content-and-site-controls","content":"The contextual site controls also expose the page's engine, Reader and content blocking where the engine offers them, permissions, extension actions, and developer status. On Chromium pages, blocking ads and trackers comes from the extensions you install. Decisions for camera, microphone, automatic downloads, popups, or external-app handoff are remembered within the current Space."},"230":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","type":"page","content":"Use Peek and Quick Window","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Browse faster"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window"},"231":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-0","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","content":"Preview links without losing your place and handle links opened from other apps."},"232":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-1","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window#peek","content":"Peek"},"233":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-2","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window#pull-a-link-into-peek-on-mac","content":"Pull a link into Peek on Mac"},"234":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-3","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window#quick-window","content":"Quick Window"},"235":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-4","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window#sign-in-and-other-popup-windows","content":"Sign-in and other popup windows"},"236":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-5","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window#shared-windows-and-blank-window-on-mac","content":"Shared windows and Blank Window on Mac"},"237":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-6","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window#cleanup-and-remembered-destinations","content":"Cleanup and remembered destinations"},"238":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-7","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","content":"Peek and Quick Window are transient browsing surfaces. Both use a real Crest Space profile so the page can access the right signed-in session and Crest Passwords, but neither has to become a durable tab."},"239":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-8","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window#peek","content":"Peek opens a link above the source page. Close it to return immediately, or choose **Open In…** to promote it into a full tab in the current Space or another one. **Command-W** closes an open Peek and **Command-O** promotes it."},"240":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-9","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window#peek","content":"In **Settings → Links**, you can automatically open cross-site links from pinned and saved tabs in Peek. You can also choose whether **Option-click** or **Command-click** explicitly opens Peek; the other modifier opens the link in a new tab."},"241":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-10","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window#peek","content":"Peek stays attached to its source tab when you open another tab or switch Spaces. Return to the source tab to continue in its Peek. If the source is one card in Split View, promotion and page commands follow that focused card."},"242":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-11","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window#pull-a-link-into-peek-on-mac","content":"Drag a webpage link to pull out a live preview that follows your gesture and fades in as the page loads. Release to keep the preview open, then close it or promote it into a tab using Peek’s controls."},"243":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-12","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window#pull-a-link-into-peek-on-mac","content":"Choose this behavior in **Settings → Links → Drag links to Peek**. Hold **Option** to drag the link normally; when the setting is off, Option-drag opens Peek instead."},"244":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-13","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window#pull-a-link-into-peek-on-mac","content":"On iPhone and iPad, touch and hold webpage links for the native link preview and actions, including opening a link in another Space. Touch and hold an image for image actions such as saving it."},"245":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-14","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window#quick-window","content":"Quick Window carries forward the idea behind Arc's Tiny Arc. It handles a link from another app without dropping it immediately into the durable sidebar. It uses the configured Space’s cookies and passwords. When the page matters, move it into a normal window and choose the right Space."},"246":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-15","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window#quick-window","content":"Open a blank Quick Window with **Option-Shift-Command-N** on Mac. In **Settings → Links**, choose whether external links use Quick Window, the most recent Space, or a chosen Space."},"247":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-16","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window#sign-in-and-other-popup-windows","content":"When a page opens a popup window, like a **Sign in with Google** or **Sign in with Apple** window, Crest for Mac shows it in a Quick Window in the same Space. The popup stays connected to the page that opened it, uses the same engine as that page, and closes itself when the sign-in finishes. Choose **Open in** and the Space to keep it as a tab instead, or close the Quick Window to drop it. A page that opens a new tab, rather than a popup window, still opens a tab beside it. On iPhone and iPad, a popup opens as a tab."},"248":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-17","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window#shared-windows-and-blank-window-on-mac","content":"Use **Command-N** for another window onto your shared Spaces and tabs. Each window keeps its own selected Space and tab. Organizing or closing a tab changes the shared workspace; closing the window itself keeps your tabs available in the other windows."},"249":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-18","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window#shared-windows-and-blank-window-on-mac","content":"When two windows show the same tab, the focused window holds the live page and the other displays its preview. Focus the other window to continue there with the same page state."},"250":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-19","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window#shared-windows-and-blank-window-on-mac","content":"Use **Option-Command-N** for a **New Blank Window**: a disposable workspace using the current Space's cookies, passwords, extensions, and settings. Its tabs, folders, history, and archive are temporary, stay out of iCloud sync, and are discarded when the window closes. It shares the Space's signed-in website session; use a Private Space when you need temporary website storage too."},"251":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-20","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window#shared-windows-and-blank-window-on-mac","content":"Drag a tab outside the window to move it into a blank window at the drop location. Move a tab back into a normal window to keep it in the shared workspace."},"252":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-21","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window#cleanup-and-remembered-destinations","content":"Quick Window records can auto-archive after **1, 6, 12, or 24 hours**, or remain until you remove them. Enable **Remember the chosen Space for each site** when repeated links from the same domain should return to the destination you previously chose."},"253":{"id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window-22","page_id":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/peek-and-quick-window#cleanup-and-remembered-destinations","content":"Archived Quick Windows remain distinguishable in Archive so you can recover something you dismissed too quickly."},"254":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","type":"page","content":"Extension compatibility","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Compatibility & troubleshooting"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility"},"255":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-0","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","content":"Which extensions Crest runs, where, and which Chrome extension features Crest connects to its own interface."},"256":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-1","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#where-extensions-run","content":"Where extensions run"},"257":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-2","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#packages","content":"Packages"},"258":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-3","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#browser-features-extensions-use","content":"Browser features extensions use"},"259":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-4","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#known-limits","content":"Known limits"},"260":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-5","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","content":"Extensions in Crest for Mac run on the Chromium engine. Chromium runs each extension itself, with its own background service worker, APIs and permission checks, so an extension behaves much as it does in Chrome. Crest connects the parts that appear in a browser window, such as the toolbar, popups, side panels and shortcuts, to its own interface."},"261":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-6","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#where-extensions-run","content":"| Where                           | Extensions                                  |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| Chromium pages in Crest for Mac | Chrome extensions from the Chrome Web Store |","table":"table-0"},"262":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-7","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#where-extensions-run","content":"| Where                         | Extensions |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------- |\n| WebKit pages in Crest for Mac | None       |","table":"table-0"},"263":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-8","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#where-extensions-run","content":"| Where                    | Extensions |\n| ------------------------ | ---------- |\n| Crest on iPhone and iPad | None       |","table":"table-0"},"264":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-9","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#where-extensions-run","content":"Crest does not install Firefox add-ons or Safari Web Extensions. Many of them also publish a Chrome version. See Firefox add-ons and Safari Web Extensions."},"265":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-10","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#packages","content":"| Package                     | Support                                                                                                            |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Chrome Web Store extensions | Supported. Chromium checks the publisher's signature and the extension's ID before Crest shows its install review. |","table":"table-1"},"266":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-11","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#packages","content":"| Package                           | Support                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Extensions in more than one Space | Each Space gets its own installation and data. A copy reuses your approval only when the extension's identity, version and permission warnings match what you reviewed. |","table":"table-1"},"267":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-12","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#packages","content":"| Package             | Support                                                                                                                                  |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Unpacked extensions | For development. Install them from Chromium's extension manager in developer mode, linked from each Space's Extensions page in Settings. |","table":"table-1"},"268":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-13","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#packages","content":"| Package                 | Support        |\n| ----------------------- | -------------- |\n| Firefox `.xpi` packages | Not supported. |","table":"table-1"},"269":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-14","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#packages","content":"| Package                                                               | Support        |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| Safari Web Extensions, Safari content blockers, Safari App Extensions | Not supported. |","table":"table-1"},"270":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-15","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#browser-features-extensions-use","content":"| Feature                    | In Crest                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Toolbar actions and popups | The action appears in the Space's extension strip or in Site Controls. Its popup opens below the button in a window attached to the Crest window. Pinned actions belong to the Space, so they appear even on the Start Page. |","table":"table-2"},"271":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-16","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#browser-features-extensions-use","content":"| Feature     | In Crest                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Side panels | `chrome.sidePanel` opens as a card beside the page it belongs to. The action's context menu, an icon click set to open the panel, and `sidePanel.open()` and `close()` all reach that card. |","table":"table-2"},"272":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-17","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#browser-features-extensions-use","content":"| Feature            | In Crest                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Keyboard shortcuts | `chrome.commands` shortcuts work when Crest's own shortcuts do not use the same keys. Change them on Chromium's extension shortcuts page, linked from each Space's Extensions page in Settings. See Set extension keyboard shortcuts. |","table":"table-2"},"273":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-18","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#browser-features-extensions-use","content":"| Feature     | In Crest                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| New windows | `chrome.windows.create` opens a Crest window in the Space that owns the extension's profile. A popup window, such as a password manager's popout, opens as a tab in the current window instead, and the extension can still find, move and close it as its own window. A requested window state is ignored. A request no Space can host fails with an error. |","table":"table-2"},"274":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-19","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#browser-features-extensions-use","content":"| Feature    | In Crest                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Tab groups | A group an extension makes with `chrome.tabs.group` or `chrome.tabGroups` appears as a folder in the Space's open tabs, with the group's name and color. Renaming, recoloring, collapsing or deleting the folder, or moving tabs into or out of it, changes the group, and the extension sees the change. A pinned or saved tab an extension groups stays where it is. After Crest restarts, the folder keeps following the group, which comes back under the same ID as its tabs load. This Mac keeps the link between folder and group; it does not sync to your other devices. |","table":"table-2"},"275":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-20","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#browser-features-extensions-use","content":"| Feature    | In Crest                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Signing in | `chrome.identity.launchWebAuthFlow` returns to the extension's own sign-in address, as in Chrome, so an extension that signs you back in on its own, such as Claude, stays signed in after Crest restarts. |","table":"table-2"},"276":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-21","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#browser-features-extensions-use","content":"| Feature         | In Crest                                                                   |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Private windows | Private windows use separate profiles and do not run installed extensions. |","table":"table-2"},"277":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-22","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#browser-features-extensions-use","content":"| Feature                        | In Crest                                                                                       |\n| ------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Tab sharing and debugging bars | Chromium's confirmation bars, such as the one `chrome.debugger` shows, appear inside the page. |","table":"table-2"},"278":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-23","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#browser-features-extensions-use","content":"| Feature | In Crest                                                                                  |\n| ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Updates | Chromium updates Chrome Web Store extensions and checks their signatures and permissions. |","table":"table-2"},"279":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-24","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#browser-features-extensions-use","content":"| Feature               | In Crest                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Native companion apps | Supported through `nativeMessaging`. When a companion app registered its helper only for Google Chrome, Crest also looks in Chrome's locations. A helper still answers only the extensions it lists. See Native companions. |","table":"table-2"},"280":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-25","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#known-limits","content":"Crest's registration of the Chromium engine states that full extension API parity is not complete. Features that need a Chrome browser window Crest does not draw may be missing."},"281":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-26","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#known-limits","content":"Apple's iCloud Passwords helper checks the browser's signature and entitlements before it pairs. See iCloud Passwords in Crest."},"282":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-27","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#known-limits","content":"An extension that is still enabled but whose files are gone shows no toolbar tile or settings row, and its action reports that it is unavailable."},"283":{"id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility-28","page_id":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-api-compatibility#known-limits","content":"For package-specific native limits, continue with Native companions."},"284":{"id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","page_id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","type":"page","content":"Extension known limitations","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Compatibility & troubleshooting"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/extension-compatibility"},"285":{"id":"/guides/extension-compatibility-0","page_id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-compatibility","content":"Where extensions run in Crest, and the limits that apply to them."},"286":{"id":"/guides/extension-compatibility-1","page_id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/extension-compatibility#package-formats","content":"Package formats"},"287":{"id":"/guides/extension-compatibility-2","page_id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/extension-compatibility#spaces-and-private-windows","content":"Spaces and private windows"},"288":{"id":"/guides/extension-compatibility-3","page_id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/extension-compatibility#browser-features","content":"Browser features"},"289":{"id":"/guides/extension-compatibility-4","page_id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/extension-compatibility#companion-apps","content":"Companion apps"},"290":{"id":"/guides/extension-compatibility-5","page_id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/extension-compatibility#extensions-from-older-crest-versions","content":"Extensions from older Crest versions"},"291":{"id":"/guides/extension-compatibility-6","page_id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-compatibility","content":"Crest for Mac runs Chrome extensions from the Chrome Web Store on its Chromium engine. The extension compatibility page lists which browser features Crest connects to its interface. This page collects the limits."},"292":{"id":"/guides/extension-compatibility-7","page_id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-compatibility","content":"Extensions run only on Chromium pages in Crest for Mac. Pages you open in WebKit, including protected-video pages that switch there automatically, run without extensions, as does Crest on iPhone and iPad. Installations and settings stay in one Space on one device."},"293":{"id":"/guides/extension-compatibility-8","page_id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-compatibility#package-formats","content":"Chrome Web Store extensions install and update through Chromium."},"294":{"id":"/guides/extension-compatibility-9","page_id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-compatibility#package-formats","content":"Unpacked extensions install from Chromium's extension manager in developer mode."},"295":{"id":"/guides/extension-compatibility-10","page_id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-compatibility#package-formats","content":"Firefox add-ons, Safari Web Extensions, Safari content blockers and Safari App Extensions are not supported."},"296":{"id":"/guides/extension-compatibility-11","page_id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-compatibility#spaces-and-private-windows","content":"Each Space has its own installation and data. Copying an extension to another Space installs it fresh; its data does not follow."},"297":{"id":"/guides/extension-compatibility-12","page_id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-compatibility#spaces-and-private-windows","content":"Private windows use a fresh, separate profile and do not run installed extensions. You cannot install or remove extensions from a private window."},"298":{"id":"/guides/extension-compatibility-13","page_id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-compatibility#spaces-and-private-windows","content":"A locked Space cannot receive an extension until you unlock it."},"299":{"id":"/guides/extension-compatibility-14","page_id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-compatibility#browser-features","content":"Crest does not yet match Chrome for every extension API. A feature that needs part of Chrome's window that Crest does not draw may be missing."},"300":{"id":"/guides/extension-compatibility-15","page_id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-compatibility#browser-features","content":"A window an extension opens appears as a Crest window in the extension's Space. A requested window state, such as maximized, is ignored."},"301":{"id":"/guides/extension-compatibility-16","page_id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-compatibility#browser-features","content":"Extension shortcuts work only when Crest's own shortcuts don't use the same keys."},"302":{"id":"/guides/extension-compatibility-17","page_id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-compatibility#companion-apps","content":"Extensions that talk to a Mac app, such as password managers, depend on that app trusting Crest's signature. See Native companions, Set up 1Password in Crest and iCloud Passwords in Crest."},"303":{"id":"/guides/extension-compatibility-18","page_id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-compatibility#extensions-from-older-crest-versions","content":"Earlier versions of Crest ran extensions in WebKit through their own compatibility layer. Crest no longer runs extensions in WebKit, and those installations do not carry over. Install each extension again from the Chrome Web Store in the Space you want."},"304":{"id":"/guides/extension-compatibility-19","page_id":"/guides/extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-compatibility#extensions-from-older-crest-versions","content":"If an installed extension misbehaves, continue with Troubleshoot an extension."},"305":{"id":"/guides/extension-status","page_id":"/guides/extension-status","type":"page","content":"Check an extension's status and details","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Compatibility & troubleshooting"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/extension-status"},"306":{"id":"/guides/extension-status-0","page_id":"/guides/extension-status","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-status","content":"See whether an extension is on, and find its errors and permissions in Chromium's extension manager."},"307":{"id":"/guides/extension-status-1","page_id":"/guides/extension-status","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/extension-status#in-crest-settings","content":"In Crest Settings"},"308":{"id":"/guides/extension-status-2","page_id":"/guides/extension-status","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/extension-status#in-chromiums-extension-manager","content":"In Chromium's extension manager"},"309":{"id":"/guides/extension-status-3","page_id":"/guides/extension-status","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/extension-status#an-extension-whose-files-are-gone","content":"An extension whose files are gone"},"310":{"id":"/guides/extension-status-4","page_id":"/guides/extension-status","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-status","content":"Crest shows each extension's basic state in its own settings. Chromium's extension manager holds the detailed record: errors, permissions and site access."},"311":{"id":"/guides/extension-status-5","page_id":"/guides/extension-status","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-status#in-crest-settings","content":"Open **Crest Settings**, select the Space in the sidebar, then select **Extensions**. Each installed extension has a row with:"},"312":{"id":"/guides/extension-status-6","page_id":"/guides/extension-status","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-status#in-crest-settings","content":"its name, version and description;"},"313":{"id":"/guides/extension-status-7","page_id":"/guides/extension-status","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-status#in-crest-settings","content":"**From Chrome Web Store** for store installations;"},"314":{"id":"/guides/extension-status-8","page_id":"/guides/extension-status","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-status#in-crest-settings","content":"the **Enabled** switch. Turning it off keeps the installation and its data in the Space."},"315":{"id":"/guides/extension-status-9","page_id":"/guides/extension-status","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-status#in-crest-settings","content":"Expand the row to see the permissions and website access Chromium reports, and to reach **Extension Settings**, **Manage Permissions in Chromium**, **Install a copy in other spaces** and **Remove Extension**."},"316":{"id":"/guides/extension-status-10","page_id":"/guides/extension-status","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-status#in-chromiums-extension-manager","content":"For errors and every other detail, open the manager for the extension's Space:"},"317":{"id":"/guides/extension-status-11","page_id":"/guides/extension-status","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-status#in-chromiums-extension-manager","content":"From the extension's action menu, choose **Manage Extension…** for that extension, or **Manage Extensions…** for the whole list."},"318":{"id":"/guides/extension-status-12","page_id":"/guides/extension-status","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-status#in-chromiums-extension-manager","content":"On the Space's Extensions page in **Crest Settings**, select **Chromium Extension Manager**."},"319":{"id":"/guides/extension-status-13","page_id":"/guides/extension-status","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-status#in-chromiums-extension-manager","content":"The manager shows what Chrome's does, including errors the extension reported. Include them, with the extension version, Crest version and the steps that fail, in a bug report."},"320":{"id":"/guides/extension-status-14","page_id":"/guides/extension-status","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-status#an-extension-whose-files-are-gone","content":"If an extension is still turned on but its files are missing, Crest shows no toolbar tile and no settings row for it. Selecting its action reports that the extension is unavailable. Reinstall it from the Chrome Web Store."},"321":{"id":"/guides/extension-status-15","page_id":"/guides/extension-status","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-status#an-extension-whose-files-are-gone","content":"Continue with Troubleshoot an extension."},"322":{"id":"/guides/icloud-passwords","page_id":"/guides/icloud-passwords","type":"page","content":"iCloud Passwords in Crest","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Compatibility & troubleshooting"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/icloud-passwords"},"323":{"id":"/guides/icloud-passwords-0","page_id":"/guides/icloud-passwords","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/icloud-passwords","content":"How the iCloud Passwords extension connects to Apple's password helper in Crest for Mac, and what Apple requires."},"324":{"id":"/guides/icloud-passwords-1","page_id":"/guides/icloud-passwords","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/icloud-passwords#how-the-extension-finds-apples-helper","content":"How the extension finds Apple's helper"},"325":{"id":"/guides/icloud-passwords-2","page_id":"/guides/icloud-passwords","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/icloud-passwords#what-apple-checks","content":"What Apple checks"},"326":{"id":"/guides/icloud-passwords-3","page_id":"/guides/icloud-passwords","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/icloud-passwords#if-it-does-not-pair","content":"If it does not pair"},"327":{"id":"/guides/icloud-passwords-4","page_id":"/guides/icloud-passwords","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/icloud-passwords#official-reference","content":"Official reference"},"328":{"id":"/guides/icloud-passwords-5","page_id":"/guides/icloud-passwords","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/icloud-passwords","content":"The iCloud Passwords extension installs from the Chrome Web Store into Crest for Mac and runs on Chromium pages. It is only half of iCloud Passwords. The other half is Apple's system password helper, which the extension reaches through native messaging."},"329":{"id":"/guides/icloud-passwords-6","page_id":"/guides/icloud-passwords","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/icloud-passwords#how-the-extension-finds-apples-helper","content":"Apple registers its helper for Google Chrome. Crest checks Chrome's native-messaging folders when Chromium's own lookup finds nothing, so the extension can reach it. Chromium still checks that the helper allows this extension. Crest does not read your passwords; Apple's helper controls authentication and access to them."},"330":{"id":"/guides/icloud-passwords-7","page_id":"/guides/icloud-passwords","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/icloud-passwords#what-apple-checks","content":"Apple protects its helper with a launch constraint on the browser. The browser must carry the managed **Web Browser Public Key Credential Requests** capability, or use an identity Apple has approved. The entitlement is:"},"331":{"id":"/guides/icloud-passwords-8","page_id":"/guides/icloud-passwords","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/icloud-passwords#what-apple-checks","content":"The signed Crest release carries this entitlement. Development and review builds do not, so iCloud Passwords cannot pair in them. Adding the entitlement to a build yourself does not authorize it; Apple checks it against the app's provisioning."},"332":{"id":"/guides/icloud-passwords-9","page_id":"/guides/icloud-passwords","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/icloud-passwords#if-it-does-not-pair","content":"Confirm that you are running the signed Crest release from `/Applications`."},"333":{"id":"/guides/icloud-passwords-10","page_id":"/guides/icloud-passwords","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/icloud-passwords#if-it-does-not-pair","content":"Reinstalling the extension does not change the browser's signature or entitlements."},"334":{"id":"/guides/icloud-passwords-11","page_id":"/guides/icloud-passwords","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/icloud-passwords#if-it-does-not-pair","content":"Until it pairs, use Crest's built-in passwords for the Space or another password manager."},"335":{"id":"/guides/icloud-passwords-12","page_id":"/guides/icloud-passwords","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/icloud-passwords#official-reference","content":"Web Browser Public Key Credential entitlement"},"336":{"id":"/guides/native-companion-limits","page_id":"/guides/native-companion-limits","type":"page","content":"Native companions","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Compatibility & troubleshooting"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/native-companion-limits"},"337":{"id":"/guides/native-companion-limits-0","page_id":"/guides/native-companion-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/native-companion-limits","content":"How extensions in Crest for Mac connect to their companion Mac apps, and what those apps check."},"338":{"id":"/guides/native-companion-limits-1","page_id":"/guides/native-companion-limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/native-companion-limits#how-crest-finds-the-helper","content":"How Crest finds the helper"},"339":{"id":"/guides/native-companion-limits-2","page_id":"/guides/native-companion-limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/native-companion-limits#the-app-decides-whether-to-trust-crest","content":"The app decides whether to trust Crest"},"340":{"id":"/guides/native-companion-limits-3","page_id":"/guides/native-companion-limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/native-companion-limits#what-crest-does-not-do","content":"What Crest does not do"},"341":{"id":"/guides/native-companion-limits-4","page_id":"/guides/native-companion-limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/native-companion-limits#availability","content":"Availability"},"342":{"id":"/guides/native-companion-limits-5","page_id":"/guides/native-companion-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/native-companion-limits","content":"Most extensions need no desktop helper. A smaller group, with password managers the common example, uses `nativeMessaging` to talk to a separate Mac app."},"343":{"id":"/guides/native-companion-limits-6","page_id":"/guides/native-companion-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/native-companion-limits#how-crest-finds-the-helper","content":"Extensions run on Chromium, which handles `nativeMessaging` as Chrome does. Each companion app registers a small manifest that names its helper and the extension IDs it will answer."},"344":{"id":"/guides/native-companion-limits-7","page_id":"/guides/native-companion-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/native-companion-limits#how-crest-finds-the-helper","content":"Most companion apps register only with Google Chrome. When Chromium's own lookup finds no manifest, Crest also checks Chrome's per-user and system `NativeMessagingHosts` folders. Chromium still checks the manifest's `allowed_origins`, so a helper answers only the extensions its app lists."},"345":{"id":"/guides/native-companion-limits-8","page_id":"/guides/native-companion-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/native-companion-limits#the-app-decides-whether-to-trust-crest","content":"Some companion apps check the browser's code signature before they answer."},"346":{"id":"/guides/native-companion-limits-9","page_id":"/guides/native-companion-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/native-companion-limits#the-app-decides-whether-to-trust-crest","content":"**1Password** accepts a browser you add through its **Add Browser** setting, and checks that browser's signature. See Set up 1Password in Crest."},"347":{"id":"/guides/native-companion-limits-10","page_id":"/guides/native-companion-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/native-companion-limits#the-app-decides-whether-to-trust-crest","content":"**iCloud Passwords** uses Apple's password helper, which Apple protects with a launch constraint on the browser's identity and entitlements. See iCloud Passwords in Crest."},"348":{"id":"/guides/native-companion-limits-11","page_id":"/guides/native-companion-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/native-companion-limits#the-app-decides-whether-to-trust-crest","content":"Use the signed and notarized Crest release in `/Applications`. A development build carries a different signature, and companion apps that check the signature reject it."},"349":{"id":"/guides/native-companion-limits-12","page_id":"/guides/native-companion-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/native-companion-limits#what-crest-does-not-do","content":"Crest does not copy Chrome's profile or read a companion app's data."},"350":{"id":"/guides/native-companion-limits-13","page_id":"/guides/native-companion-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/native-companion-limits#what-crest-does-not-do","content":"Safari app extensions and their native handlers do not work in Crest."},"351":{"id":"/guides/native-companion-limits-14","page_id":"/guides/native-companion-limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/native-companion-limits#availability","content":"Official Crest for Mac builds are signed with Developer ID, notarized, and published through GitHub Releases, with updates through a signed Sparkle appcast."},"352":{"id":"/guides/onepassword","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","type":"page","content":"Set up 1Password in Crest","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Compatibility & troubleshooting"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/onepassword"},"353":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-0","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/onepassword","content":"Install the 1Password Chrome extension in Crest for Mac and authorize Crest in the 1Password app."},"354":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-1","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/onepassword#before-you-begin","content":"Before you begin"},"355":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-2","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/onepassword#install-the-extension","content":"Install the extension"},"356":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-3","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/onepassword#authorize-crest-in-1password","content":"Authorize Crest in 1Password"},"357":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-4","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/onepassword#if-it-does-not-connect","content":"If it does not connect"},"358":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-5","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/onepassword#official-references","content":"Official references"},"359":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-6","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/onepassword","content":"The 1Password Chrome Web Store extension runs on Chromium pages in Crest for Mac. To unlock and fill through the 1Password app, the app must trust Crest as a browser."},"360":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-7","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/onepassword","content":"1Password checks the browser's code signature. Use the Developer ID signed and notarized Crest release installed in `/Applications`. A development build carries a different signature, and 1Password rejects it."},"361":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-8","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/onepassword#before-you-begin","content":"Install and unlock **1Password for Mac**."},"362":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-9","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/onepassword#before-you-begin","content":"Switch to the Crest Space that should own the extension. Installations do not copy to another Space or device on their own."},"363":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-10","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/onepassword#install-the-extension","content":"In Crest for Mac, open the 1Password page in the Chrome Web Store."},"364":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-11","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/onepassword#install-the-extension","content":"Select **Add to Crest**."},"365":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-12","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/onepassword#install-the-extension","content":"Review the package, its permissions and the destination Space in Crest's review sheet."},"366":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-13","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/onepassword#install-the-extension","content":"Select **Add Extension**, then **Done**."},"367":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-14","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/onepassword#authorize-crest-in-1password","content":"Open and unlock **1Password for Mac**."},"368":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-15","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/onepassword#authorize-crest-in-1password","content":"Select your account or collection at the top of the sidebar, then select **Settings**."},"369":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-16","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/onepassword#authorize-crest-in-1password","content":"Select **Browser** in the sidebar."},"370":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-17","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/onepassword#authorize-crest-in-1password","content":"Select **Add Browser**."},"371":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-18","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/onepassword#authorize-crest-in-1password","content":"Choose **Crest** in `/Applications`."},"372":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-19","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/onepassword#authorize-crest-in-1password","content":"Review 1Password's access prompt and select **Authorize**."},"373":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-20","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/onepassword#authorize-crest-in-1password","content":"1Password warns that an additional browser can reach your saved information while 1Password is unlocked, so it can save and fill logins. Only authorize a Crest build you trust."},"374":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-21","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/onepassword#if-it-does-not-connect","content":"Reinstalling the extension does not change the signature 1Password checks. Confirm that you added the Crest app in `/Applications`, then see Native companions and Troubleshoot an extension."},"375":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-22","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/onepassword#official-references","content":"Connect additional browsers to the 1Password app"},"376":{"id":"/guides/onepassword-23","page_id":"/guides/onepassword","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/onepassword#official-references","content":"1Password browser code-signature requirements"},"377":{"id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility","page_id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility","type":"page","content":"Troubleshoot an extension","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Compatibility & troubleshooting"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility"},"378":{"id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility-0","page_id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility","content":"Steps to try when a Chrome extension installs in Crest but a feature does not work."},"379":{"id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility-1","page_id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility#try-these-first","content":"Try these first"},"380":{"id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility-2","page_id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility#read-the-error","content":"Read the error"},"381":{"id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility-3","page_id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility#in-a-private-window","content":"In a private window"},"382":{"id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility-4","page_id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility#password-managers-and-companion-apps","content":"Password managers and companion apps"},"383":{"id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility-5","page_id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility#features-crest-draws-differently","content":"Features Crest draws differently"},"384":{"id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility-6","page_id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility","content":"Extensions run on Chromium, so most behave as they do in Chrome. When one doesn't, the cause is usually its Space, its site access, or a browser feature Crest draws differently from Chrome."},"385":{"id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility-7","page_id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility#try-these-first","content":"Check that you are in the Space where you installed it. Each Space has its own installations. See Spaces and profile isolation."},"386":{"id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility-8","page_id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility#try-these-first","content":"In **Crest Settings**, select the Space in the sidebar, then **Extensions**. Turn the extension off and back on."},"387":{"id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility-9","page_id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility#try-these-first","content":"Expand its row, select **Manage Permissions in Chromium**, and check whether its site access covers the page you are on."},"388":{"id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility-10","page_id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility#try-these-first","content":"Open **Extension Settings** if the extension has them, and check its own options."},"389":{"id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility-11","page_id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility#try-these-first","content":"Remove the extension and install it again from the Chrome Web Store."},"390":{"id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility-12","page_id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility#read-the-error","content":"Choose **Manage Extension…** from the extension's action menu to open Chromium's extension manager. It lists errors the extension reported. See Check an extension's status and details."},"391":{"id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility-13","page_id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility#in-a-private-window","content":"Private windows use a fresh profile and do not inherit a Space's installed extensions. You cannot install or remove extensions there. Test the extension in its normal Space instead; enabling Chrome's incognito option does not copy it into Crest's separate private profile."},"392":{"id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility-14","page_id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility#password-managers-and-companion-apps","content":"If the extension needs a Mac app, such as 1Password or iCloud Passwords, the app decides whether to trust Crest. Use the signed and notarized Crest release, not a development build. See Native companions."},"393":{"id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility-15","page_id":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/troubleshoot-extension-compatibility#features-crest-draws-differently","content":"Crest shows popups, side panels, extension windows and keyboard shortcuts in its own interface. An extension that expects part of Chrome's window that Crest does not draw may lose that feature. See Extension compatibility."},"394":{"id":"/guides/engines","page_id":"/guides/engines","type":"page","content":"Chromium and WebKit on Mac","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/engines"},"395":{"id":"/guides/engines-0","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines","content":"Choose the engine new pages open in, send a website to the other engine, and see what each engine supports."},"396":{"id":"/guides/engines-1","page_id":"/guides/engines","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/engines#chromium","content":"Chromium"},"397":{"id":"/guides/engines-2","page_id":"/guides/engines","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/engines#choose-the-default-engine","content":"Choose the default engine"},"398":{"id":"/guides/engines-3","page_id":"/guides/engines","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/engines#open-a-website-in-the-other-engine","content":"Open a website in the other engine"},"399":{"id":"/guides/engines-4","page_id":"/guides/engines","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/engines#website-rules","content":"Website rules"},"400":{"id":"/guides/engines-5","page_id":"/guides/engines","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/engines#protected-video","content":"Protected video"},"401":{"id":"/guides/engines-6","page_id":"/guides/engines","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/engines#after-updating-from-a-webkit-only-crest","content":"After updating from a WebKit-only Crest"},"402":{"id":"/guides/engines-7","page_id":"/guides/engines","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/engines#what-each-engine-supports","content":"What each engine supports"},"403":{"id":"/guides/engines-8","page_id":"/guides/engines","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/engines#current-chromium-limits","content":"Current Chromium limits"},"404":{"id":"/guides/engines-9","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines","content":"Crest for Mac includes two web engines. New pages open in Chromium unless you choose otherwise, and any website or page can use WebKit, the engine behind Safari. Crest on iPhone and iPad uses WebKit."},"405":{"id":"/guides/engines-10","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines","content":"Your Spaces, tabs, history, passwords and settings are the same whichever engine shows a page. Website data is not: each engine keeps its own cookies and storage for a Space, so signing in to a site in Chromium does not sign you in to it in WebKit."},"406":{"id":"/guides/engines-11","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#chromium","content":"Crest's Chromium engine is built on ungoogled-chromium, which removes Google integrations from Chromium. It runs Chrome Web Store extensions."},"407":{"id":"/guides/engines-12","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#chromium","content":"Chromium starts the first time you need it. If WebKit is your default and no page uses Chromium, it stays unloaded. Opening a Chromium page or an extension starts it, and it stays running until you quit Crest."},"408":{"id":"/guides/engines-13","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#choose-the-default-engine","content":"Open **Crest Settings → Engines**."},"409":{"id":"/guides/engines-14","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#choose-the-default-engine","content":"Select **Chromium** or **WebKit**."},"410":{"id":"/guides/engines-15","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#choose-the-default-engine","content":"The default applies to pages you open afterwards. Open pages keep their engine, and links a page opens stay on that page's engine. Select **Use Recommended Default** to return to Chromium."},"411":{"id":"/guides/engines-16","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#open-a-website-in-the-other-engine","content":"**For one page:** choose **Page → Open Page in WebKit** or **Open Page in Chromium**. The page reloads in the other engine. Other pages from the site keep opening where they did."},"412":{"id":"/guides/engines-17","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#open-a-website-in-the-other-engine","content":"**For a whole website:** open Site Controls and change **Opens in**. The page reloads in that engine, and later pages from the website open there too."},"413":{"id":"/guides/engines-18","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#open-a-website-in-the-other-engine","content":"A tab whose page runs in the engine that is not your default shows that engine's mark on its icon."},"414":{"id":"/guides/engines-19","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#website-rules","content":"Choosing **Opens in** saves a website rule. Rules are listed under **Crest Settings → Engines → Website rules**, where you can:"},"415":{"id":"/guides/engines-20","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#website-rules","content":"select **Add Website Rule…** to send a website to an engine before you visit it;"},"416":{"id":"/guides/engines-21","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#website-rules","content":"select a rule to change its website or engine;"},"417":{"id":"/guides/engines-22","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#website-rules","content":"select **Remove Rule** to return a website to your default engine."},"418":{"id":"/guides/engines-23","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#website-rules","content":"Rules match the website's scheme, host and port. A rule for `example.com` does not cover its subdomains. A choice made while browsing privately is not saved as a rule; it lasts until you quit Crest."},"419":{"id":"/guides/engines-24","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#protected-video","content":"Chromium in Crest cannot play DRM-protected video. When a page asks for it, Crest automatically switches to WebKit to try Apple's FairPlay support, unless you have explicitly chosen an engine for that website. The switch checks for unsaved work first. Choosing **Stay on Page** keeps the page in Chromium and leaves its website rule unchanged; repeated requests from that document do not prompt again. After an allowed move, the website opens in WebKit on later visits. Select **Move Back** to return it to Chromium, or remove its rule in Settings. Playback still depends on the site's support for FairPlay."},"420":{"id":"/guides/engines-25","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#after-updating-from-a-webkit-only-crest","content":"The previous stable 0.6 release used WebKit only. Updating to Crest 0.7 keeps your Spaces, tabs, history and Crest Passwords. New pages open in Chromium unless you choose WebKit as your default. Each engine keeps separate website data, so Chromium does not inherit your WebKit sign-ins. Your existing WebKit website data remains available to pages opened in WebKit."},"421":{"id":"/guides/engines-26","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#after-updating-from-a-webkit-only-crest","content":"Extensions installed in earlier versions do not carry over. Install them again from the Chrome Web Store."},"422":{"id":"/guides/engines-27","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#what-each-engine-supports","content":"| Feature                     | Chromium | WebKit |\n| --------------------------- | -------- | ------ |\n| Chrome Web Store extensions | Yes      | No     |","table":"table-0"},"423":{"id":"/guides/engines-28","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#what-each-engine-supports","content":"| Feature | Chromium | WebKit |\n| ------- | -------- | ------ |\n| Reader  | No       | Yes    |","table":"table-0"},"424":{"id":"/guides/engines-29","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#what-each-engine-supports","content":"| Feature                          | Chromium                      | WebKit |\n| -------------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ------ |\n| Built-in ad and tracker blocking | No. Use a blocking extension. | Yes    |","table":"table-0"},"425":{"id":"/guides/engines-30","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#what-each-engine-supports","content":"| Feature         | Chromium                                                      | WebKit                                 |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| Protected video | Automatically switches to WebKit after unsaved-changes checks | FairPlay, when the website supports it |","table":"table-0"},"426":{"id":"/guides/engines-31","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#what-each-engine-supports","content":"| Feature      | Chromium                    | WebKit                         |\n| ------------ | --------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| Find in Page | Shows the number of matches | Shows whether there is a match |","table":"table-0"},"427":{"id":"/guides/engines-32","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#what-each-engine-supports","content":"| Feature          | Chromium      | WebKit             |\n| ---------------- | ------------- | ------------------ |\n| Save Web Archive | `.mhtml` file | `.webarchive` file |","table":"table-0"},"428":{"id":"/guides/engines-33","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#what-each-engine-supports","content":"| Feature        | Chromium          | WebKit        |\n| -------------- | ----------------- | ------------- |\n| Inspect a page | Chromium DevTools | Web Inspector |","table":"table-0"},"429":{"id":"/guides/engines-34","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#what-each-engine-supports","content":"Tabs, Spaces, Split View, Peek, Crest Passwords, site permissions, Picture in Picture and downloads are available in both. Their engine controls can differ; Chromium downloads also offer pause and resume. See Translate, read, and use page tools and Downloads for details."},"430":{"id":"/guides/engines-35","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#current-chromium-limits","content":"Crest Passwords handles saved passwords. Built-in address and payment-card autofill are not available."},"431":{"id":"/guides/engines-36","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#current-chromium-limits","content":"Screen sharing offers your tabs in the same Space first, with their audio when the site asks for it. A window or your screen goes through the macOS picker, which shares no audio."},"432":{"id":"/guides/engines-37","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#current-chromium-limits","content":"Local service-worker and extension notifications work while Crest runs. Remote Web Push is not available."},"433":{"id":"/guides/engines-38","page_id":"/guides/engines","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/engines#current-chromium-limits","content":"See Site permissions and notifications for permission controls and the Google-free engine's site and download protection limits."},"434":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","type":"page","content":"Install and update Crest for Mac","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac"},"435":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-0","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","content":"Download Crest directly, install it in Applications, and understand automatic updates."},"436":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-1","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#install-the-latest-mac-release","content":"Install the latest Mac release"},"437":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-2","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#automatic-updates","content":"Automatic updates"},"438":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-3","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#update-channels","content":"Update channels"},"439":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-4","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#updating-from-an-older-crest","content":"Updating from an older Crest"},"440":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-5","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#iphone-and-ipad","content":"iPhone and iPad"},"441":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-6","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","content":"Crest for Mac requires Apple silicon and macOS 26.1 or later. It is distributed directly as a signed and notarized app with Chromium and WebKit; see Chromium and WebKit on Mac. Crest for iPhone and iPad is on the App Store and continues to use WebKit."},"442":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-7","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#install-the-latest-mac-release","content":"Open the latest stable Crest release."},"443":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-8","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#install-the-latest-mac-release","content":"Download its `Installer-….dmg` file."},"444":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-9","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#install-the-latest-mac-release","content":"Open the disk image, then drag Crest into **Applications**."},"445":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-10","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#install-the-latest-mac-release","content":"Eject the disk image and open Crest from Applications."},"446":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-11","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#install-the-latest-mac-release","content":"Alternatively, Crest can be installed via Homebrew:"},"447":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-12","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#install-the-latest-mac-release","content":"Open Terminal."},"448":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-13","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#install-the-latest-mac-release","content":"Run `brew install --cask crest-browser`"},"449":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-14","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#install-the-latest-mac-release","content":"Keeping Crest in Applications gives macOS and the updater one stable installed location. If Gatekeeper reports that the app cannot be verified, do not bypass the warning; download the current release again from the official Releases page."},"450":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-15","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#automatic-updates","content":"Crest uses Sparkle to check for signed updates from inside the installed app. When an update is available, review the release, install it, and let Crest relaunch. Your Spaces and browsing data remain in their normal app storage rather than inside the application bundle."},"451":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-16","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#automatic-updates","content":"Turn automatic checks and installs on or off in **Settings → About**, which also has **Check for Updates…**. You can also open the app menu and choose **Check for Updates**. A manual check uses the same signed update channel as the automatic check."},"452":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-17","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#update-channels","content":"Use **Settings → About** to choose the update channel:"},"453":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-18","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#update-channels","content":"**Stable** is the normal public release cadence."},"454":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-19","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#update-channels","content":"**Nightly** receives newer builds sooner and can change more frequently."},"455":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-20","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#update-channels","content":"**Development** follows the latest signed public `main` build and can change several times a day."},"456":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-21","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#update-channels","content":"Changing channels changes which future update is offered; it does not move or duplicate your profile."},"457":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-22","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#updating-from-an-older-crest","content":"The same installer updates older WebKit-only versions and versions that already include Chromium. Your Spaces and browser records stay in place. Chromium and WebKit keep separate website sign-ins, and older WebKit extension installations do not carry over. See Upgrading from a WebKit-only Crest before switching engines."},"458":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-23","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#updating-from-an-older-crest","content":"Crest checks pages for unsaved work before an update restart. Choose **Stay on Page** to keep working, then retry the restart when ready. Updates are offered only when your Mac meets the whole app's macOS requirement."},"459":{"id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac-24","page_id":"/guides/install-and-update-mac","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-and-update-mac#iphone-and-ipad","content":"Install Crest for iPhone and iPad from the App Store, or join the beta through TestFlight. If iCloud sync is enabled, the same durable Space structure can follow you between Mac, iPad, and iPhone."},"460":{"id":"/guides/move-to-crest","page_id":"/guides/move-to-crest","type":"page","content":"Move your browser data to Crest","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/move-to-crest"},"461":{"id":"/guides/move-to-crest-0","page_id":"/guides/move-to-crest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/move-to-crest","content":"Review imports from Arc, Zen, Chrome, Safari, Firefox, and other Chromium browsers, and export portable Crest data."},"462":{"id":"/guides/move-to-crest-1","page_id":"/guides/move-to-crest","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/move-to-crest#import-during-setup","content":"Import during setup"},"463":{"id":"/guides/move-to-crest-2","page_id":"/guides/move-to-crest","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/move-to-crest#import-later","content":"Import later"},"464":{"id":"/guides/move-to-crest-3","page_id":"/guides/move-to-crest","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/move-to-crest#export-a-portable-backup","content":"Export a portable backup"},"465":{"id":"/guides/move-to-crest-4","page_id":"/guides/move-to-crest","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/move-to-crest#after-import","content":"After import"},"466":{"id":"/guides/move-to-crest-5","page_id":"/guides/move-to-crest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/move-to-crest","content":"Browser-to-browser import runs on Mac. Crest prepares a visual review first so you can decide what arrives and where it belongs before the live session changes."},"467":{"id":"/guides/move-to-crest-6","page_id":"/guides/move-to-crest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/move-to-crest#import-during-setup","content":"Choose one or more detected browsers, then review each source Space, profile, or window. Depending on what that browser exposes, Crest can bring across Spaces or profiles, tabs, bookmarks, saved folders, split views, tab groups, colors, icons, extensions, and supported passwords."},"468":{"id":"/guides/move-to-crest-7","page_id":"/guides/move-to-crest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/move-to-crest#import-during-setup","content":"| Source | Crest can review                                                                       |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Arc    | Spaces, tabs, folders, split views, colors, icons, extensions, and supported passwords |","table":"table-0"},"469":{"id":"/guides/move-to-crest-8","page_id":"/guides/move-to-crest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/move-to-crest#import-during-setup","content":"| Source | Crest can review                                                                                       |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Zen    | Spaces from every profile, Essentials, pinned tabs, folders, split views, open tabs, icons, and colors |","table":"table-0"},"470":{"id":"/guides/move-to-crest-9","page_id":"/guides/move-to-crest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/move-to-crest#import-during-setup","content":"| Source | Crest can review                                                                             |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Chrome | Profiles, bookmarks, open tabs, tab groups, split views, extensions, and supported passwords |","table":"table-0"},"471":{"id":"/guides/move-to-crest-10","page_id":"/guides/move-to-crest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/move-to-crest#import-during-setup","content":"| Source                                                                                               | Crest can review                                                                             |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Brave, Edge, Vivaldi, Opera, Dia, Comet, Aside, ego lite, Chromium, and Chrome Beta, Dev, and Canary | Profiles, bookmarks, open tabs, tab groups, split views, extensions, and supported passwords |","table":"table-0"},"472":{"id":"/guides/move-to-crest-11","page_id":"/guides/move-to-crest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/move-to-crest#import-during-setup","content":"| Source | Crest can review                               |\n| ------ | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| Safari | Bookmarks, windows, open tabs, and pinned tabs |","table":"table-0"},"473":{"id":"/guides/move-to-crest-12","page_id":"/guides/move-to-crest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/move-to-crest#import-during-setup","content":"| Source  | Crest can review                                          |\n| ------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Firefox | Profiles, windows, open tabs, pinned tabs, and tab groups |","table":"table-0"},"474":{"id":"/guides/move-to-crest-13","page_id":"/guides/move-to-crest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/move-to-crest#import-during-setup","content":"If your browser isn't listed, choose **Browser not listed?** and Crest looks for other Chromium-based browsers on your Mac. Not every browser can be found this way; you can request support for one."},"475":{"id":"/guides/move-to-crest-14","page_id":"/guides/move-to-crest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/move-to-crest#import-during-setup","content":"In the review, each Space shows the Chrome Web Store extensions it brings under its address bar. Turn off any you don't want, and Crest installs the rest once the import finishes, without asking about each one."},"476":{"id":"/guides/move-to-crest-15","page_id":"/guides/move-to-crest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/move-to-crest#import-during-setup","content":"For every source group, you can remove individual items, choose a new or existing Crest Space, and include supported passwords only when you want them. Choose **Customize** to rename the destination and edit its colors, crest, and Banner or Traditional Gradient style before importing. The before-and-after preview updates as you decide. When an import holds more than Crest keeps, it brings what fits and lists what it left out."},"477":{"id":"/guides/move-to-crest-16","page_id":"/guides/move-to-crest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/move-to-crest#import-later","content":"Open **Settings → Advanced**. The **Import & Export** section can import a Crest archive, bookmark HTML, browser history, or open tabs from supported sources. External-browser imports always create fresh isolated Crest Spaces unless the review explicitly routes content into an existing destination."},"478":{"id":"/guides/move-to-crest-17","page_id":"/guides/move-to-crest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/move-to-crest#export-a-portable-backup","content":"Choose **Export Browser Data…** in **Settings → Advanced**. A Crest archive includes Spaces, folders, saved and current tabs, Archive, history, and browsing preferences."},"479":{"id":"/guides/move-to-crest-18","page_id":"/guides/move-to-crest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/move-to-crest#export-a-portable-backup","content":"For safety, the portable archive does not contain passwords, cookies, website storage, site permissions, downloaded files, favicons, or extensions. Password export is a separate, device-authenticated plaintext operation: select a Space in the Settings sidebar, then choose **Passwords → Export Passwords…**. Treat that file as sensitive."},"480":{"id":"/guides/move-to-crest-19","page_id":"/guides/move-to-crest","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/move-to-crest#after-import","content":"Browse each new Space once before removing data from your old browser. Check signed-in state, saved locations, folder nesting, and any critical extension workflow. If iCloud sync is enabled, imported Spaces and tabs can then follow you to iPad and iPhone."},"481":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","type":"page","content":"Settings reference","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/settings-reference"},"482":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-0","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference","content":"Find every major Crest setting and understand whether it applies globally or to one Space."},"483":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-1","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/settings-reference#general","content":"General"},"484":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-2","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/settings-reference#tabs","content":"Tabs"},"485":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-3","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/settings-reference#search","content":"Search"},"486":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-4","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/settings-reference#appearance","content":"Appearance"},"487":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-5","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/settings-reference#links","content":"Links"},"488":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-6","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/settings-reference#engines","content":"Engines"},"489":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-7","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/settings-reference#shortcuts","content":"Shortcuts"},"490":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-8","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/settings-reference#sync","content":"Sync"},"491":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-9","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/settings-reference#privacy","content":"Privacy"},"492":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-10","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/settings-reference#spaces","content":"Spaces"},"493":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-11","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/settings-reference#add-arrange-and-remove-spaces","content":"Add, arrange, and remove Spaces"},"494":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-12","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/settings-reference#agents","content":"Agents"},"495":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-13","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/settings-reference#advanced","content":"Advanced"},"496":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-14","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/settings-reference#about","content":"About"},"497":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-15","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/settings-reference#iphone-and-ipad","content":"iPhone and iPad"},"498":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-16","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference","content":"Open **Crest → Settings** on Mac. On iPhone and iPad, open Settings from the browser interface. Some controls appear only on the platform that supports them."},"499":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-17","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference","content":"On Mac and wider iPad windows, Settings opens as a browser tab and keeps your place when you switch away. In compact layouts, including iPhone, it opens as a dismissible sheet while your current page stays selected."},"500":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-18","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference","content":"On Mac, the Settings sidebar lists General, Tabs, Search, Appearance, Links, Engines, Shortcuts, Sync, and Privacy, then each of your Spaces by name and crest, then Agents, Advanced and About. iPhone and iPad keep their own layout; see iPhone and iPad."},"501":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-19","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#general","content":"Make Crest your default browser, choose what happens when Crest opens, and pick the default Space. General also holds automatic page translation and spell checking. On Mac, it includes **Picture in Picture when switching tabs** and **Developer toolbar on local pages**. On iPhone and iPad, **Start on new tab** opens Crest on a new tab in the default Space, and **Allow floating sidebar** lets the sidebar float over the page instead of filling the screen."},"502":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-20","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#tabs","content":"Choose whether tabs opened from links get focus with **Switch to tabs opened from links**, and whether to **Follow tabs moved to another Space**. Set what pinned and saved tabs do after you close them, and whether clicking the favicon returns to the saved URL. Tabs also holds sidebar widgets and, on Mac, Split View's **Focus follows pointer** and **Show recent tabs while switching**, which shows your recent tabs while you hold Control-Tab."},"503":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-21","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#search","content":"**Default search**: the search engine or AI assistant every Space uses unless it chose its own, the one **Private windows** use, and whether the default gives **Search suggestions**. **Tab to search providers** lets Tab choose a provider by its name or shortcut in the command palette, and **Space to search providers** lets a space after `$` and a shortcut, or after a shortcut alone, choose it."},"504":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-22","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#search","content":"The command palette settings come next:"},"505":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-23","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#search","content":"**Results**: show results under a header for each kind or **Blended** into one list, lead with a **Top Hit**, prefer an open tab over history for the same site, and **Show match reasons**, which notes under each result why it is there, such as \"Often visited\"."},"506":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-24","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#search","content":"**Sections**: turn each kind of result on or off, choose how many results each shows, and drag them into the order you want; **Reset Order** puts them back. Before you type, **Recent Tabs** and **Actions** show in this order."},"507":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-25","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#search","content":"**Also show**: **Settings Pages**, **@ Filters** such as `@tabs`, the **Calculator** and, on Mac, **Paste and Go**, which offers the address you copied when the palette opens."},"508":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-26","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#search","content":"**Typing**: complete addresses inline and learn from the results you choose. **Clear Learned Choices** forgets what the palette learned. Learned choices stay on this device."},"509":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-27","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#search","content":"The search providers come last:"},"510":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-28","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#search","content":"**Search Engines**, **AI Assistants** and **Websites**: every provider Crest offers, each with its main shortcut. Turn a provider off to stop its shortcut; the default stays on. Click a provider to open it and see its options, such as Google's **Hide AI Overviews** or ChatGPT's **Model**, and to change its shortcuts."},"511":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-29","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#search","content":"**Add Provider…** adds your own search engine, AI assistant or website with a name, shortcuts, search URL and color. **Restore Defaults…** puts the built-in providers' shortcuts and options back; providers you added stay."},"512":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-30","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#search","content":"Search providers and their settings stay on this device."},"513":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-31","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#search","content":"See Use the command palette."},"514":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-32","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#appearance","content":"Customize the browser on this device with a live preview. Choose sidebar position, the window border, tab shape and scale, pinned-tab layout, address-field style, folder display, and an app icon palette. With **Follow Space accent** on, selected tabs, pins, and the address field use the current Space's color; turn it off to pick a custom color. **Default page zoom** offers fixed levels from **50% to 300%**. Use presets to get started or reset individual changed settings."},"515":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-33","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#appearance","content":"A Space's crest, colors, and sidebar background live on the Space's Appearance page. See Spaces and Customize and arrange Spaces."},"516":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-34","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#links","content":"Choose what happens to links from other apps, which Space supplies their signed-in session, and how long Quick Windows remain recoverable. Under Peek, choose whether eligible links from pinned or saved pages open in Peek, which modifier click opens it, and, on Mac, whether to **Drag links to Peek**. Link Routing rules live here too."},"517":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-35","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#engines","content":"On Mac, choose whether new pages open in Chromium or WebKit, and manage website rules that send particular websites to one engine. Chromium is the recommended default. See Chromium and WebKit on Mac."},"518":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-36","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#shortcuts","content":"Search the complete Mac command catalog, record a replacement, inspect conflicts, clear an assignment, or restore the default. Extension shortcuts are set on Chromium's extension shortcuts page, opened from **Shortcuts…** on a Space's Extensions page, because they belong to the extension installed in that Space."},"519":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-37","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#sync","content":"Enable or disable iCloud sync and review its current state. Private Spaces and transient browsing are intentionally excluded."},"520":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-38","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#privacy","content":"On Mac, Privacy covers the whole device. **System permissions** shows whether macOS lets Crest use the camera, microphone, location, notifications, passkeys, and files and folders. Below that, select a Space to open its Privacy page, where its data retention, content blocking, and site permissions live."},"521":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-39","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#spaces","content":"On Mac, every Space has its own page. Select the Space in the Settings sidebar; the window switches to that Space, and Settings follows. The page header shows the Space's crest and name. Hover over the name and click the pencil to rename it, or open the **…** menu for more actions."},"522":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-40","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#spaces","content":"Each Space's page has these tabs:"},"523":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-41","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#spaces","content":"**Appearance**: Crest Studio for the Space's crest, colors, and sidebar background."},"524":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-42","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#spaces","content":"**Browsing**: **Search with** and **Search suggestions**, which follow your default search until you choose for the Space, archiving old tabs with **Archive current tabs** and **Archive Now**, downloads (whether to ask where to save, and the download folder), and **Delete Space**."},"525":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-43","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#spaces","content":"**Privacy**: **Require Touch ID or password**, how long to keep History, Archived Tabs, and Download Records, content blocking, and saved site permissions."},"526":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-44","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#spaces","content":"**Passwords**: **Use Crest Passwords**, **Sync with iCloud Keychain**, and the Space's saved passwords, with **Import Passwords…** and **Export Passwords…**."},"527":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-45","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#spaces","content":"**Extensions**: available when Chromium is. **Open Chrome Web Store**, **Chromium Extension Manager**, **Shortcuts…**, and the extensions installed in the Space."},"528":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-46","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#add-arrange-and-remove-spaces","content":"Click **+** next to the Spaces heading to add a Space. Its Appearance page opens with the name ready to type. Click the pencil next to it to rearrange: drag Spaces by their handles, then click the checkmark when done."},"529":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-47","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#add-arrange-and-remove-spaces","content":"Right-click a Space, or use the **…** menu on its page, for **Rename**, **Edit Crest…**, **Move Up**, **Move Down**, **Lock Space**, and **Delete**. Crest needs at least one Space."},"530":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-48","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#agents","content":"On Mac, choose whether coding agents on your Mac may use Crest, which Spaces they reach, and whether they may run scripts in pages; connect an agent, and see the agents connected now and the ones you allowed. See Let coding agents use Crest."},"531":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-49","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#advanced","content":"Import and export browser data, access runtime and diagnostic controls, and manage developer-facing behavior. Change advanced options deliberately; many of them exist to diagnose a specific browser or engine condition rather than improve everyday browsing."},"532":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-50","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#advanced","content":"On Mac, the **Feature Flags** row opens Chromium's feature flags for the current Space. Use the back arrow to return to Advanced."},"533":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-51","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#advanced","content":"Choose **Rerun onboarding** to return to Welcome and go through setup again. Completing setup opens Getting Started in your first Space, reusing its existing guide when available."},"534":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-52","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#about","content":"**About** shows Crest’s build information and links to the community. On Mac, it also holds software updates: automatic checks and installs, the update channel, and **Check for Updates…**."},"535":{"id":"/guides/settings-reference-53","page_id":"/guides/settings-reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/settings-reference#iphone-and-ipad","content":"iPhone and iPad keep their own Settings navigation, with the same **Tabs** and **Appearance** pages for the whole device. **Spaces** is a page of its own: choose a Space from its picker to customize it and set its browsing and cleanup choices. **Privacy** also has a Space picker for data retention, content blocking, and site permissions. **Passwords** lists Crest Passwords by Space; authenticate to reveal or export them, and choose whether eligible credentials sync with iCloud Keychain."},"536":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","type":"page","content":"Install from the Chrome Web Store","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Install extensions"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store"},"537":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-0","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","content":"Add a Chrome extension from its store page to the current Crest Space."},"538":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-1","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#before-you-add-it","content":"Before you add it"},"539":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-2","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#install-the-extension","content":"Install the extension"},"540":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-3","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#use-it-after-installation","content":"Use it after installation"},"541":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-4","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#updates","content":"Updates"},"542":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-5","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#when-you-cant-install","content":"When you can't install"},"543":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-6","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","content":"Crest for Mac installs Chrome extensions from the Chrome Web Store. Extensions run on Chromium pages. Pages you open in WebKit, and Crest on iPhone and iPad, run no extensions."},"544":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-7","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#before-you-add-it","content":"Switch to the Space that should own the extension. Its package, enablement, permissions, storage and pinning stay separate from every other Space and device."},"545":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-8","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#install-the-extension","content":"In a normal Crest window on Mac, open the extension's page in the **Chrome Web Store**."},"546":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-9","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#install-the-extension","content":"Select the store's own button, which reads **Add to Crest**. You can also open **Site Controls** and select **Install Extension…**."},"547":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-10","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#install-the-extension","content":"Wait while Crest downloads the package from Google's update service. Chromium checks the publisher's signature and the extension's ID before the review appears."},"548":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-11","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#install-the-extension","content":"In the review sheet, check the extension's name and the **Verified Chrome Web Store package** label."},"549":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-12","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#install-the-extension","content":"Open **Review Access and Compatibility** and read the permission warnings. Where the extension allows it, turn on **Withhold website access until I grant it**."},"550":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-13","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#install-the-extension","content":"To install the same package in more Spaces, select **Install in other Spaces…** and choose them."},"551":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-14","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#install-the-extension","content":"Select **Add Extension**, then **Done**."},"552":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-15","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#install-the-extension","content":"Once installed, the listing's button reads **Added to Crest**, and it offers **Remove from Crest** for this Space."},"553":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-16","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#use-it-after-installation","content":"Open **Site Controls** beside the address field to find the extension's action, and pin it if you want it in the Space's extension strip. See Pin extensions and use popups."},"554":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-17","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#use-it-after-installation","content":"Open **Crest Settings**, select the Space in the sidebar, then select **Extensions**. Expand the extension to turn it on or off, open its settings, manage its permissions, copy it to other Spaces, or remove it."},"555":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-18","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#use-it-after-installation","content":"If the extension has keyboard commands, see Set extension keyboard shortcuts."},"556":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-19","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#updates","content":"Chromium updates Chrome Web Store extensions on its own and checks each update's signature and permissions, as Chrome does."},"557":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-20","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#when-you-cant-install","content":"Private windows keep the store's own behavior and do not offer **Add to Crest**."},"558":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-21","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#when-you-cant-install","content":"A locked Space, or one that has been deleted, cannot receive an extension or a copy."},"559":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-22","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#when-you-cant-install","content":"Crest does not install Firefox add-ons or Safari Web Extensions. Look for the extension's Chrome version."},"560":{"id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store-23","page_id":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-chrome-web-store#when-you-cant-install","content":"Next: Manage permissions and website access."},"561":{"id":"/guides/install-firefox-add-ons","page_id":"/guides/install-firefox-add-ons","type":"page","content":"Firefox add-ons","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Install extensions"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/install-firefox-add-ons"},"562":{"id":"/guides/install-firefox-add-ons-0","page_id":"/guides/install-firefox-add-ons","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-firefox-add-ons","content":"Crest does not install Firefox add-ons. Use an extension's Chrome Web Store version instead."},"563":{"id":"/guides/install-firefox-add-ons-1","page_id":"/guides/install-firefox-add-ons","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-firefox-add-ons","content":"Crest does not install Firefox add-ons from **addons.mozilla.org**."},"564":{"id":"/guides/install-firefox-add-ons-2","page_id":"/guides/install-firefox-add-ons","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-firefox-add-ons","content":"Extensions in Crest for Mac run on the Chromium engine, which runs Chrome extensions from the Chrome Web Store. It cannot load a Firefox `.xpi` package. WebKit pages, and Crest on iPhone and iPad, run no extensions."},"565":{"id":"/guides/install-firefox-add-ons-3","page_id":"/guides/install-firefox-add-ons","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-firefox-add-ons","content":"Many Firefox add-ons also publish a Chrome version. Look for the same extension in the Chrome Web Store and install it from there. See Install from the Chrome Web Store."},"566":{"id":"/guides/install-firefox-add-ons-4","page_id":"/guides/install-firefox-add-ons","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/install-firefox-add-ons","content":"If you installed Firefox add-ons in an earlier version of Crest, they do not carry over. Install each extension's Chrome version into the Space you want."},"567":{"id":"/guides/scan-safari-web-extensions","page_id":"/guides/scan-safari-web-extensions","type":"page","content":"Safari Web Extensions","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Install extensions"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/scan-safari-web-extensions"},"568":{"id":"/guides/scan-safari-web-extensions-0","page_id":"/guides/scan-safari-web-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/scan-safari-web-extensions","content":"Crest does not scan Mac apps for Safari Web Extensions. Use an extension's Chrome Web Store version instead."},"569":{"id":"/guides/scan-safari-web-extensions-1","page_id":"/guides/scan-safari-web-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/scan-safari-web-extensions","content":"Crest does not scan the apps on your Mac for Safari Web Extensions, and it cannot add one from an app bundle."},"570":{"id":"/guides/scan-safari-web-extensions-2","page_id":"/guides/scan-safari-web-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/scan-safari-web-extensions","content":"Extensions in Crest for Mac run on the Chromium engine, which installs Chrome extensions from the Chrome Web Store. A Safari Web Extension ships inside a Mac app in Safari's format, and Chromium does not load it. WebKit pages, and Crest on iPhone and iPad, run no extensions."},"571":{"id":"/guides/scan-safari-web-extensions-3","page_id":"/guides/scan-safari-web-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/scan-safari-web-extensions","content":"Many Safari Web Extensions also publish a Chrome version. Look for the same extension in the Chrome Web Store and install it from there. See Install from the Chrome Web Store."},"572":{"id":"/guides/scan-safari-web-extensions-4","page_id":"/guides/scan-safari-web-extensions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/scan-safari-web-extensions","content":"Safari content blockers and legacy Safari App Extensions are separate formats, and Crest does not support them either."},"573":{"id":"/guides/clear-website-data","page_id":"/guides/clear-website-data","type":"page","content":"Clear website data","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Privacy, data & recovery"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/clear-website-data"},"574":{"id":"/guides/clear-website-data-0","page_id":"/guides/clear-website-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/clear-website-data","content":"Clear one site's cookies or cache, manage each Space's website data, and clear browsing data by time range."},"575":{"id":"/guides/clear-website-data-1","page_id":"/guides/clear-website-data","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/clear-website-data#clear-one-site","content":"Clear one site"},"576":{"id":"/guides/clear-website-data-2","page_id":"/guides/clear-website-data","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/clear-website-data#manage-a-spaces-website-data","content":"Manage a Space's website data"},"577":{"id":"/guides/clear-website-data-3","page_id":"/guides/clear-website-data","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/clear-website-data#clear-browsing-data","content":"Clear browsing data"},"578":{"id":"/guides/clear-website-data-4","page_id":"/guides/clear-website-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/clear-website-data","content":"Website data belongs to the Space that stored it, and it stays on this device. Clearing it in one Space never touches another Space, your saved passwords, extensions, downloaded files, or site permissions."},"579":{"id":"/guides/clear-website-data-5","page_id":"/guides/clear-website-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/clear-website-data#clear-one-site","content":"Open Site Controls beside the address and choose:"},"580":{"id":"/guides/clear-website-data-6","page_id":"/guides/clear-website-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/clear-website-data#clear-one-site","content":"**Clear Cookies** removes the site's cookies and everything else it stored in the Space: local storage, IndexedDB, Cache Storage and service workers, including what sites embedded in it stored there. It signs you out of the site."},"581":{"id":"/guides/clear-website-data-7","page_id":"/guides/clear-website-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/clear-website-data#clear-one-site","content":"**Clear Cache** removes only the responses Crest kept to load the site faster."},"582":{"id":"/guides/clear-website-data-8","page_id":"/guides/clear-website-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/clear-website-data#clear-one-site","content":"Crest clears the whole site, such as `example.com` and its subdomains, in both engines, reloads the page, and shows the result at the top of the window. The same actions are in the command palette as **Clear Cookies for This Site** and **Clear Cache for This Site**, and on iPhone and iPad in the page menu. In a private window, they clear only what that window holds in memory."},"583":{"id":"/guides/clear-website-data-9","page_id":"/guides/clear-website-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/clear-website-data#manage-a-spaces-website-data","content":"On Mac, open Settings, select the Space, then select **Privacy**. On iPhone and iPad, open **Settings → Privacy** and choose the Space. **Website data** lists the sites that keep data in the Space and what each keeps. Choose **Remove** for one site, or **Remove All…** for every site in the Space."},"584":{"id":"/guides/clear-website-data-10","page_id":"/guides/clear-website-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/clear-website-data#clear-browsing-data","content":"Below Website data, **Clear browsing data** removes what the Space browsed within a time range, from **Last Hour** to **All Time**. Choose any of **History**, **Cookies and Site Data**, and **Cached Images and Files**, then **Clear…**. Clearing history in a Space that syncs removes it from your other devices too."},"585":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","type":"page","content":"Content blocking and site permissions","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Privacy, data & recovery"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions"},"586":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-0","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","content":"Control ads, trackers, camera, microphone, pop-ups, downloads, and external apps per Space."},"587":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-1","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#content-blocking","content":"Content blocking"},"588":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-2","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#malicious-sites-and-downloads","content":"Malicious sites and downloads"},"589":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-3","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#site-permissions","content":"Site permissions"},"590":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-4","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#notifications","content":"Notifications"},"591":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-5","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#reset-a-site","content":"Reset a site"},"592":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-6","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#extension-site-access","content":"Extension site access"},"593":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-7","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","content":"Privacy decisions belong to the current Space. A permission granted to a work account does not silently become a permission for the same host in Personal."},"594":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-8","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#content-blocking","content":"Crest includes a small built-in ad and tracker ruleset that can be enabled or disabled per Space. It uses WebKit, so it applies on iPhone, iPad, and WebKit pages on Mac. Use the site controls or assign **Toggle Content Blocking** a shortcut when a site needs a quick exception."},"595":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-9","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#content-blocking","content":"To change it for a Space, turn **Block known ads and trackers** on or off in that Space’s privacy settings. On Mac, open Settings, select the Space in the sidebar, then select **Privacy**. On iPhone and iPad, open **Settings → Privacy** and choose the Space."},"596":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-10","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#content-blocking","content":"Chromium pages on Mac have no built-in blocking. Install a content-blocking extension, such as uBlock Origin Lite, in each Space that needs it. Extensions do not run on WebKit pages."},"597":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-11","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#content-blocking","content":"For broader filter-list coverage, install a content-blocking extension in the Space that needs it. Built-in protection and an extension can have different rule coverage, so check which layer is active before assuming the page itself is broken."},"598":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-12","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#malicious-sites-and-downloads","content":"Crest's Chromium build keeps Google services disabled and does not include Google Safe Browsing or another built-in site and download reputation service. It cannot warn about every known phishing site or malicious download. Certificate checks, Chromium's sandbox, and warnings about executable or insecure downloads remain in place. Those checks do not determine whether a file is malware, and a completed download is not a safety verdict."},"599":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-13","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#site-permissions","content":"Crest can remember decisions for:"},"600":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-14","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#site-permissions","content":"Camera"},"601":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-15","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#site-permissions","content":"Microphone"},"602":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-16","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#site-permissions","content":"Camera and microphone together"},"603":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-17","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#site-permissions","content":"Location"},"604":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-18","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#site-permissions","content":"Notifications"},"605":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-19","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#site-permissions","content":"Pop-ups"},"606":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-20","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#site-permissions","content":"Automatic downloads"},"607":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-21","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#site-permissions","content":"Opening external apps"},"608":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-22","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#site-permissions","content":"Open Site Controls on the affected page to inspect or reset the decision. The Space’s privacy settings, in the same place as content blocking, list its saved site permissions."},"609":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-23","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#site-permissions","content":"Screen sharing asks what to share each time. You can block it for a site, but cannot preapprove a tab, screen or window. On pages that run in Chromium on Mac, Crest first lists the tabs in the same Space, and can share a tab's audio. Choose Window or Screen to use the macOS picker instead, which shares no audio. While a tab is shared, it and the sharing page show a bar with Stop sharing, and the shared tab is outlined in the sidebar. Minimize a bar to hide it until you come back to that tab. To stop from the sidebar, right-click either tab and choose Stop Sharing. Clicking the sharing symbol on a shared tab also offers to go to the tab it is shared to."},"610":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-24","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#notifications","content":"Allow the site in Crest and allow Crest in macOS notification settings to receive notifications. On Mac, **Settings → Privacy → System permissions** shows whether macOS allows it. Document notifications belong to their open page. Chromium also supports local service-worker and extension notifications while Crest runs, including a service worker's notification after its tab closes. Private profiles do not deliver these background notifications. Locking a Space or revoking its site permission withdraws notifications it can no longer show."},"611":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-25","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#notifications","content":"Remote Web Push delivery is not available in this Google-free Chromium build. Local service-worker notifications do not mean that a site can receive server pushes or wake Crest after it quits."},"612":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-26","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#reset-a-site","content":"If a site behaves as though an old choice still applies, first reset its saved permission rather than deleting the entire Space. Clearing a site's data is broader: it signs you out and removes what the site stored in that Space."},"613":{"id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions-27","page_id":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/content-blocking-and-site-permissions#extension-site-access","content":"Extension permissions are a separate layer. An extension may be installed but still blocked from the current host, or it may require approval for additional sites. See Manage extension permissions and site access for the extension-specific controls."},"614":{"id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads","page_id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads","type":"page","content":"History, Archive, downloads, and retention","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Privacy, data & recovery"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads"},"615":{"id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads-0","page_id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads","content":"Search, restore, remove, and retain browser records independently in each Space."},"616":{"id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads-1","page_id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads#history","content":"History"},"617":{"id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads-2","page_id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads#archive","content":"Archive"},"618":{"id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads-3","page_id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads#downloads","content":"Downloads"},"619":{"id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads-4","page_id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads#retention-per-space","content":"Retention per Space"},"620":{"id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads-5","page_id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads","content":"History, Archive, and Downloads are common browser surfaces, but every record remains attached to the Space that created it."},"621":{"id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads-6","page_id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads#history","content":"Open History with **Command-Y**, the menu, or the command palette. Search visits in the current Space and reopen a result. The command palette also includes relevant history matches while you type."},"622":{"id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads-7","page_id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads#archive","content":"Archive contains manually closed or archived tabs, automatic Space cleanup, and expired Quick Windows. Filter by reason when you know how the item left the sidebar. Restoring an archived tab returns it to an appropriate live position in that Space."},"623":{"id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads-8","page_id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads#archive","content":"Use **Command-E** to archive the current tab, **Shift-Command-T** to reopen the last closed tab, and **Shift-Command-K** to clear unpinned current tabs into Archive."},"624":{"id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads-9","page_id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads#downloads","content":"Open Downloads with **Shift-Command-J**. Crest tracks status, destination, failures, and blocked automatic downloads. On Mac, each Space chooses its download folder, and whether to ask where to save each download, on its Browsing page in Settings. Removing or expiring a download record does not delete the downloaded file from disk."},"625":{"id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads-10","page_id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads#downloads","content":"Chromium downloads offer **Pause Download** while transferring and **Resume Download** when the engine can continue a paused or interrupted transfer. Depending on the server, resuming may restart the file. The same download record keeps its chosen destination. Cancel ends the transfer; removing a failed record does not retry it. WebKit downloads do not offer these pause and resume controls."},"626":{"id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads-11","page_id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads#downloads","content":"An unsafe-file warning requires its own decision. Resuming a transfer does not approve a warning or bypass a block. See Malicious sites and downloads for the limits of Chromium's Google-free protection."},"627":{"id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads-12","page_id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads#retention-per-space","content":"On Mac, open Settings, select the Space in the sidebar, then select **Privacy**. On iPhone and iPad, open **Settings → Privacy** and choose the Space. Choose **1 Day, 1 Week, 30 Days, 90 Days, 1 Year, or Forever** independently for History, Archived Tabs, and Download Records."},"628":{"id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads-13","page_id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads#retention-per-space","content":"Crest checks retention when it opens, after sync, and every 15 minutes while active. Shortening a duration can permanently remove older synchronized records, so Crest confirms the destructive change first."},"629":{"id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads-14","page_id":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/history-archive-and-downloads#retention-per-space","content":"Current-tab automatic cleanup is a different setting, **Archive current tabs** on the Space’s Browsing page on Mac. It archives old unpinned tabs after the chosen interval, keeping them recoverable until the Archive retention policy later expires them."},"630":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","type":"page","content":"Turn Crest Passwords on or off per Space","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Spaces & organization"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space"},"631":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-0","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","content":"Control Crest-owned password suggestions, generation, and save prompts independently for every Space."},"632":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-1","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space#change-the-setting","content":"Change the setting"},"633":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-2","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space#related-controls","content":"Related controls"},"634":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-3","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space#storage-and-deletion","content":"Storage and deletion"},"635":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-4","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","content":"Crest Passwords are private to the Space that owns them. You can stop using Crest-owned suggestions, generation, and save prompts in one Space without deleting its saved passwords or changing another Space."},"636":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-5","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space#change-the-setting","content":"On Mac:"},"637":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-6","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space#change-the-setting","content":"Open **Crest Settings** and select the Space in the sidebar."},"638":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-7","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space#change-the-setting","content":"Select **Passwords**."},"639":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-8","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space#change-the-setting","content":"Turn **Use Crest Passwords** on or off."},"640":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-9","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space#change-the-setting","content":"On iPhone and iPad:"},"641":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-10","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space#change-the-setting","content":"Open **Settings → Passwords**."},"642":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-11","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space#change-the-setting","content":"Choose the Space you want to change from the **Space** menu."},"643":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-12","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space#change-the-setting","content":"Turn **Use Crest Passwords** on or off."},"644":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-13","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space#change-the-setting","content":"When Crest Passwords is off, saved passwords remain in that Space until you delete them. Turning the setting back on makes them available to matching sites again."},"645":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-14","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space#related-controls","content":"The same page lists the Space’s saved passwords, with **Import Passwords…** and **Export Passwords…**. When Crest Passwords is on, supported Mac builds can also show:"},"646":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-15","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space#related-controls","content":"**Sync with iCloud Keychain**, which updates whether existing and future Crest credentials in that Space synchronize through the system Keychain."},"647":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-16","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space#related-controls","content":"**Offer a copy to Passwords**, which lets the system Passwords app ask separately for a copy after Crest saves in the Space."},"648":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-17","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space#related-controls","content":"System Passwords and passkeys are provider-managed and may appear in any Space for a matching site. They are separate from Crest Passwords’ Space-local records. On Mac, check Crest’s access to system passkeys in **Settings → Privacy → System permissions → Passkeys**."},"649":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-18","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space#related-controls","content":"It does not delete saved passwords, export them, move them to another Space, or place password values in CloudKit session data."},"650":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-19","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space#related-controls","content":"Private Spaces must be unlocked before Crest reveals account and site metadata or changes their password settings."},"651":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-20","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space#storage-and-deletion","content":"Crest Passwords are saved in the system Keychain and suggested only for matching websites. Viewing, copying, or exporting a password can require device authentication."},"652":{"id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space-21","page_id":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/crest-passwords-per-space#storage-and-deletion","content":"Deleting a saved password, clearing a site's data, and deleting a whole Space are separate actions, and each shows what it removes before it proceeds."},"653":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","type":"page","content":"Customize and arrange Spaces","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Spaces & organization"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/customize-spaces"},"654":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-0","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/customize-spaces","content":"Design a Space in Crest Studio, customize its folders, and choose its browsing and cleanup settings."},"655":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-1","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/customize-spaces#choose-an-identity","content":"Choose an identity"},"656":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-2","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/customize-spaces#customize-folders","content":"Customize folders"},"657":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-3","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/customize-spaces#customize-the-browser-around-your-spaces","content":"Customize the browser around your Spaces"},"658":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-4","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/customize-spaces#add-and-arrange-spaces","content":"Add and arrange Spaces"},"659":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-5","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/customize-spaces#automatic-cleanup","content":"Automatic cleanup"},"660":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-6","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/customize-spaces","content":"Open a Space’s context menu to edit it, or open its page in Settings. On Mac, select the Space in the Settings sidebar; on iPhone and iPad, choose it in **Settings → Spaces**. A strong visual identity makes a profile boundary obvious before you type a password or open a work account."},"661":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-7","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/customize-spaces#choose-an-identity","content":"Crest offers two presentation styles:"},"662":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-8","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/customize-spaces#choose-an-identity","content":"**Banner** uses Crest Studio: begin with a template, then choose a shape, field division, pattern, trim, and heraldic artwork. Use independent colors for the parts of your design, or make an identity with an emoji, monogram, or searchable SF Symbol."},"663":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-9","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/customize-spaces#choose-an-identity","content":"**Traditional Gradient** keeps the familiar Arc-style theme: it blends one to three colors with direction, intensity, a readability fade, and optional texture."},"664":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-10","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/customize-spaces#choose-an-identity","content":"The result appears in the Space picker and browser chrome on Mac, iPad, and iPhone."},"665":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-11","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/customize-spaces#choose-an-identity","content":"Crest Studio is on the Space’s Appearance page. The crest sits on the Space’s own sidebar background, with its colors named by what they paint:"},"666":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-12","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/customize-spaces#choose-an-identity","content":"**Crest:** Field, Second field, Band, Emblem, Border and Edge. A color for a part the crest doesn’t draw is dimmed."},"667":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-13","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/customize-spaces#choose-an-identity","content":"**Sidebar:** Background, Accent (selected tabs, pins, the address field and the Space picker) and Pattern."},"668":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-14","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/customize-spaces#choose-an-identity","content":"Click or tap a color to choose one of the templates’ tinctures or a custom color. Below the crest, work through **Start from**, **Shape**, **Field**, **Band**, **Emblem**, **Border**, **Finish** and **Sidebar**; each step shows your crest with each choice applied. On iPhone, the steps are a list showing what each has chosen; tap one to open it. Choose **Icon** at the top of **Emblem** to use an SF Symbol or emoji instead of a crest. **Shuffle** suggests a new crest in the templates’ colors, and **Undo** steps back through your changes. **Reset Appearance** and **Artwork Credits** are in the **…** menu on the Space’s page."},"669":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-15","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/customize-spaces#customize-folders","content":"Choose folder color intensity and text color on the Space’s Appearance page. Individual folder menus let you set colors, search the full SF Symbols catalog, or choose emoji. You can show a custom icon on its own instead of the animated folder artwork. In **Settings → Appearance**, enable **Tint Folder Title** to use semibold titles in the folder’s color, adjusted for stronger contrast against light or dark sidebars."},"670":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-16","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/customize-spaces#customize-the-browser-around-your-spaces","content":"Open **Settings → Appearance** for device-wide appearance: a left- or right-side sidebar, borderless pages, tab shape and scale, pinned-tab layout, address-field colors, and a default page zoom from **50% to 300%**. Selected tabs, pins, and the address field follow the current Space’s color; turn off **Follow Space accent** to pick a custom color instead. Presets and a live preview help you find a starting point; each changed setting has its own reset."},"671":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-17","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/customize-spaces#customize-the-browser-around-your-spaces","content":"Choose an app icon palette here too. These controls change the browser on this device; a Space’s identity belongs to that Space and stays on its own Appearance page."},"672":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-18","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/customize-spaces#add-and-arrange-spaces","content":"On Mac, click **+** next to the Spaces heading in the Settings sidebar to add a Space. Its Appearance page opens with the name ready to type. Right-click a Space there, or use the **…** menu on its page, to rename it, edit its crest, lock it, or delete it. Crest needs at least one Space."},"673":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-19","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/customize-spaces#add-and-arrange-spaces","content":"Drag a Space in the picker to reorder it. In the Mac Settings sidebar, click the pencil next to the Spaces heading, drag Spaces by their handles, then click the checkmark; or right-click a Space and choose **Move Up** or **Move Down**. On iPhone and iPad, use the order controls in **Settings → Spaces**. Position matters for **Control-1** through **Control-9**, so put frequently used Spaces first."},"674":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-20","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/customize-spaces#automatic-cleanup","content":"Each Space can archive unpinned current tabs after **12 hours, 24 hours, 7 days, or 30 days**, or keep them until you close them. On Mac, set this with **Archive current tabs** on the Space’s Browsing page, and choose **Archive Now** to run it right away. Cleanup moves tabs into the recoverable Archive; it does not silently erase them."},"675":{"id":"/guides/customize-spaces-21","page_id":"/guides/customize-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/customize-spaces#automatic-cleanup","content":"Pinned sites, saved tabs, folders, and tabs marked **Keep Loaded** have different roles from ordinary current tabs. Use a saved tab for something you intend to revisit, and Keep Loaded only when the live in-page state matters."},"676":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","type":"page","content":"Organize tabs, saved pages, and folders","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Spaces & organization"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders"},"677":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-0","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","content":"Use current tabs, pinned sites, saved locations, folders, Archive, and Keep Loaded deliberately."},"678":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-1","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#current-tabs","content":"Current tabs"},"679":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-2","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#pinned-sites","content":"Pinned sites"},"680":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-3","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#saved-tabs-and-saved-locations","content":"Saved tabs and saved locations"},"681":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-4","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#folders","content":"Folders"},"682":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-5","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#context-menu-actions","content":"Context-menu actions"},"683":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-6","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#tab-icons","content":"Tab icons"},"684":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-7","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#organize-several-items-at-once","content":"Organize several items at once"},"685":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-8","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#clear-open-tabs","content":"Clear open tabs"},"686":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-9","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#keep-loaded-and-unload","content":"Keep Loaded and unload"},"687":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-10","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","content":"Crest uses a few distinct kinds of tab so temporary work and lasting structure do not become the same pile."},"688":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-11","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#current-tabs","content":"An ordinary page appears in the current-tabs area. Close or archive it when finished, or let the Space’s cleanup policy move old unpinned tabs into Archive."},"689":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-12","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#pinned-sites","content":"Pinned sites appear as a compact icon grid near the top of a Space. Use them for always-close destinations such as mail, calendar, or a dashboard. Choose **Pin or Unpin Current Tab** or press **Command-D**. You can also right-click a tab and choose **Pin Tab**, or right-click a pinned tab and choose **Unpin Tab**; on iPhone and iPad, touch and hold the tab instead."},"690":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-13","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#saved-tabs-and-saved-locations","content":"A saved tab belongs to the durable sidebar, optionally inside a folder. Its saved location is a home URL: you can navigate away, then double-click the saved-location indicator or use the context menu to return home. The context menu can replace or reset that saved location."},"691":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-14","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#folders","content":"Folders work in both Saved and Current Tabs. Rename them, choose a color or symbol, collapse them, nest them, and reorder their contents. Drag a complete folder between the two sections to move its tabs and nested folders together. You can also use the folder menu to change sections."},"692":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-15","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#folders","content":"Both kinds restore and sync with their section. Moving a folder preserves its name, color, hierarchy, and contents. Drag a tab onto another current tab to create a folder, or use its context menu to create or choose a folder."},"693":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-16","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#folders","content":"When an extension groups tabs, as Claude does with the tabs it works in, the group appears as a current folder with the group's name and color. Editing that folder changes the group the extension sees. See Extension compatibility."},"694":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-17","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#folders","content":"Drop along a folder’s top or bottom edge to place a tab beside it, including between empty folders. Drop inside the folder to file the tab."},"695":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-18","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#context-menu-actions","content":"Right-click on Mac or touch and hold on iPhone and iPad. Depending on the item, Crest offers rename, copy link, change icon, pin, save, move to Space, add to Split View, duplicate, unload, Keep Loaded, close, archive, reset saved location, or delete."},"696":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-19","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#tab-icons","content":"A tab's icon normally follows the current website. From the tab's context menu, choose **Pull New Icon** to keep the website's current icon, **Change Icon…** to choose an emoji, or **Clear Icon** to return to the automatic website icon."},"697":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-20","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#organize-several-items-at-once","content":"Select tabs, Split View groups, and folders together to organize them in one step. On Mac, **Command-click** toggles individual items and **Shift-click** selects a range. Use the selected items’ context menu for the available batch actions, or drag the selection to its destination."},"698":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-21","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#organize-several-items-at-once","content":"On iPhone and iPad, use the selection actions in a tab or folder’s context menu. VoiceOver exposes selection actions too. A selected folder carries its nested contents with it."},"699":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-22","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#clear-open-tabs","content":"Use the archive control on the sidebar divider to clear open tabs while keeping pinned and saved tabs. Closed tabs remain recoverable in Archive, subject to the Space’s retention settings."},"700":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-23","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#keep-loaded-and-unload","content":"**Keep Loaded** protects an important live page from ordinary unloading. It is useful for an unsaved editor, a live call, or a dashboard whose in-page state matters. Crest can still respond to genuine system memory pressure."},"701":{"id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders-24","page_id":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/organize-tabs-and-folders#keep-loaded-and-unload","content":"Choose **Unload** when you want to release a page but retain its tab. On Mac, middle-clicking a current tab closes it; middle-clicking a pinned or saved item unloads its page while keeping the durable item."},"702":{"id":"/guides/private-spaces","page_id":"/guides/private-spaces","type":"page","content":"Browse with a Private Space","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Spaces & organization"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/private-spaces"},"703":{"id":"/guides/private-spaces-0","page_id":"/guides/private-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/private-spaces","content":"Understand Private Space storage, history, sync, authentication, and relocking."},"704":{"id":"/guides/private-spaces-1","page_id":"/guides/private-spaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/private-spaces#add-device-authentication","content":"Add device authentication"},"705":{"id":"/guides/private-spaces-2","page_id":"/guides/private-spaces","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/private-spaces#what-private-browsing-does-not-do","content":"What private browsing does not do"},"706":{"id":"/guides/private-spaces-3","page_id":"/guides/private-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/private-spaces","content":"Create a Private Space when the browsing session should not become part of normal durable browser state."},"707":{"id":"/guides/private-spaces-4","page_id":"/guides/private-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/private-spaces","content":"Private Spaces use non-persistent website storage. They stay out of normal history, session restoration, Archive, and ordinary Crest sync. Closing the private session discards its transient pages and website data."},"708":{"id":"/guides/private-spaces-5","page_id":"/guides/private-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/private-spaces#add-device-authentication","content":"You can require Touch ID, Face ID, or the device passcode before opening a protected Private Space. On Mac, turn on **Require Touch ID or password** on the Space’s Privacy page in Settings. Crest can relock protected content when the app leaves the foreground so another person cannot return to it from the app switcher."},"709":{"id":"/guides/private-spaces-6","page_id":"/guides/private-spaces","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/private-spaces#what-private-browsing-does-not-do","content":"Private browsing does not make you anonymous to websites, your network, an employer, or an internet provider. Files you download and information you deliberately share with a site can still leave the browser. Use the feature to control local browser persistence, not as a promise of network anonymity."},"710":{"id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","page_id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","type":"page","content":"Spaces and profile isolation","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Spaces & organization"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation"},"711":{"id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation-0","page_id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","content":"Understand how each Crest Space separates accounts, history, passwords, permissions, and website data."},"712":{"id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation-1","page_id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation#what-belongs-to-one-space","content":"What belongs to one Space"},"713":{"id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation-2","page_id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation#switch-spaces","content":"Switch Spaces"},"714":{"id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation-3","page_id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation#move-a-tab-between-spaces","content":"Move a tab between Spaces"},"715":{"id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation-4","page_id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation#delete-a-space-carefully","content":"Delete a Space carefully"},"716":{"id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation-5","page_id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","content":"A Crest Space is not only a group of tabs. It is a separate browsing profile with its own durable organization, runtime, and privacy boundary."},"717":{"id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation-6","page_id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation#what-belongs-to-one-space","content":"Signed-in website sessions, cookies, caches, local storage, and other website data. On Mac, Chromium and WebKit each keep their own copy for the Space, so a sign-in in one engine does not carry to the other."},"718":{"id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation-7","page_id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation#what-belongs-to-one-space","content":"Current, pinned, saved, grouped, and archived tabs"},"719":{"id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation-8","page_id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation#what-belongs-to-one-space","content":"Nested folders and saved locations"},"720":{"id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation-9","page_id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation#what-belongs-to-one-space","content":"History, Archive, download records, and their retention choices"},"721":{"id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation-10","page_id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation#what-belongs-to-one-space","content":"Crest Passwords and optional iCloud Keychain participation"},"722":{"id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation-11","page_id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation#what-belongs-to-one-space","content":"Site permissions and content-blocking choices"},"723":{"id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation-12","page_id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation#what-belongs-to-one-space","content":"Extensions, actions, permissions, and extension settings on Mac"},"724":{"id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation-13","page_id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation#what-belongs-to-one-space","content":"Name, symbol, gradient or crest, and sidebar appearance"},"725":{"id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation-14","page_id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation#what-belongs-to-one-space","content":"That means the same website can be signed into different accounts in Work and Personal without those sessions meeting."},"726":{"id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation-15","page_id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation#switch-spaces","content":"Select a Space from the sidebar, swipe or scroll through the Space picker, or use **Option-Command-Left/Right** on a keyboard. **Control-1** through **Control-9** selects a Space by position."},"727":{"id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation-16","page_id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation#switch-spaces","content":"Switching changes the whole browser context. The visible tabs, history search, credentials, permissions, and website process pool all follow the selected Space."},"728":{"id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation-17","page_id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation#move-a-tab-between-spaces","content":"Open the tab’s context menu and choose a destination, or drag it to another Space when the interface presents that destination. Crest moves the durable tab record and loads it inside the destination profile; it does not transfer the source Space’s cookies or signed-in session."},"729":{"id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation-18","page_id":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/spaces-and-isolation#delete-a-space-carefully","content":"Deleting a Space removes its tabs, pins, folders, Archive, history, Crest Passwords, cookies, website storage, permissions, downloads records, and extension state. Read the confirmation before continuing. If you only need less clutter, archive or move tabs instead."},"730":{"id":"/guides/split-view","page_id":"/guides/split-view","type":"page","content":"Use Split View","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Spaces & organization"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/split-view"},"731":{"id":"/guides/split-view-0","page_id":"/guides/split-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/split-view","content":"Create, focus, resize, reorder, synchronize, and separate two to four live tabs."},"732":{"id":"/guides/split-view-1","page_id":"/guides/split-view","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/split-view#create-a-split-view","content":"Create a Split View"},"733":{"id":"/guides/split-view-2","page_id":"/guides/split-view","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/split-view#focus-a-card","content":"Focus a card"},"734":{"id":"/guides/split-view-3","page_id":"/guides/split-view","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/split-view#resize-and-reorder","content":"Resize and reorder"},"735":{"id":"/guides/split-view-4","page_id":"/guides/split-view","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/split-view#remove-or-separate-tabs","content":"Remove or separate tabs"},"736":{"id":"/guides/split-view-5","page_id":"/guides/split-view","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/split-view#ipad-and-iphone","content":"iPad and iPhone"},"737":{"id":"/guides/split-view-6","page_id":"/guides/split-view","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/split-view#sync-behavior","content":"Sync behavior"},"738":{"id":"/guides/split-view-7","page_id":"/guides/split-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/split-view","content":"Split View keeps two to four live tabs in one durable sidebar group. The focused card owns the address field and page commands; the other cards remain visible and live."},"739":{"id":"/guides/split-view-8","page_id":"/guides/split-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/split-view#create-a-split-view","content":"Use any of these paths:"},"740":{"id":"/guides/split-view-9","page_id":"/guides/split-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/split-view#create-a-split-view","content":"Drag a sidebar tab onto the current page."},"741":{"id":"/guides/split-view-10","page_id":"/guides/split-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/split-view#create-a-split-view","content":"Open the tab context menu and choose the Split View action."},"742":{"id":"/guides/split-view-11","page_id":"/guides/split-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/split-view#create-a-split-view","content":"Right-click or touch and hold a page link, then choose **Open Link in Split View**."},"743":{"id":"/guides/split-view-12","page_id":"/guides/split-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/split-view#create-a-split-view","content":"Run **Split With Next Tab** from the command palette or assign it a shortcut."},"744":{"id":"/guides/split-view-13","page_id":"/guides/split-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/split-view#create-a-split-view","content":"A one-card placeholder lets you add the next tab without losing the first page."},"745":{"id":"/guides/split-view-14","page_id":"/guides/split-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/split-view#focus-a-card","content":"Click or tap a card. On a keyboard, use **Control-Command-Left** and **Control-Command-Right**. The address, Back and Forward, Reload, Find, Reader, page tools, Peek, and extension popups follow the focused card."},"746":{"id":"/guides/split-view-15","page_id":"/guides/split-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/split-view#focus-a-card","content":"On Mac, turn on **Focus follows pointer** in **Settings → Tabs** to make pointer movement choose the active card automatically."},"747":{"id":"/guides/split-view-16","page_id":"/guides/split-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/split-view#resize-and-reorder","content":"Drag a divider to resize columns on Mac or iPad. Crest remembers widths for the window. Use **Shift-Command-Left/Right** to move the focused card, or drag when the interface exposes a reordering target."},"748":{"id":"/guides/split-view-17","page_id":"/guides/split-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/split-view#resize-and-reorder","content":"In the sidebar, drag the split's header to move the whole group. Drag an individual tab row to move just that tab out of the split, into a folder, or into another Split View. The remaining tabs stay together."},"749":{"id":"/guides/split-view-18","page_id":"/guides/split-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/split-view#remove-or-separate-tabs","content":"**Remove Tab From Split** takes the focused tab out of the group. **Separate All Tabs** turns every card back into an independent tab; its default shortcut is **Option-Command-U**. Closing the focused card closes that tab while the remaining group survives."},"750":{"id":"/guides/split-view-19","page_id":"/guides/split-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/split-view#ipad-and-iphone","content":"iPad uses the same resizable column model as Mac. On iPhone, the group remains complete but one card fills the screen at a time. Swipe horizontally on the compact toolbar to page between cards; the gesture intentionally does nothing when the current tab is not in Split View."},"751":{"id":"/guides/split-view-20","page_id":"/guides/split-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/split-view#sync-behavior","content":"The durable group and its card order can sync with the Space. A receiving device adapts the presentation to its screen instead of flattening the group."},"752":{"id":"/guides/sync-across-devices","page_id":"/guides/sync-across-devices","type":"page","content":"Sync Crest across devices","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Spaces & organization"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/sync-across-devices"},"753":{"id":"/guides/sync-across-devices-0","page_id":"/guides/sync-across-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/sync-across-devices","content":"Use iCloud to synchronize durable Spaces and resolve a device-versus-cloud conflict safely."},"754":{"id":"/guides/sync-across-devices-1","page_id":"/guides/sync-across-devices","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/sync-across-devices#what-sync-carries","content":"What sync carries"},"755":{"id":"/guides/sync-across-devices-2","page_id":"/guides/sync-across-devices","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/sync-across-devices#check-status","content":"Check status"},"756":{"id":"/guides/sync-across-devices-3","page_id":"/guides/sync-across-devices","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/sync-across-devices#resolve-a-conflict","content":"Resolve a conflict"},"757":{"id":"/guides/sync-across-devices-4","page_id":"/guides/sync-across-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/sync-across-devices","content":"Open **Settings → Sync** and enable **Sync Crest with iCloud** on each device signed into the same Apple Account."},"758":{"id":"/guides/sync-across-devices-5","page_id":"/guides/sync-across-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/sync-across-devices#what-sync-carries","content":"Crest synchronizes durable browser structure such as Spaces, tabs, saved folders, Split View groups, appearance, Archive, history, and supported preferences. Mac, iPad, and iPhone then render the same model in an interface suited to the screen."},"759":{"id":"/guides/sync-across-devices-6","page_id":"/guides/sync-across-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/sync-across-devices#what-sync-carries","content":"Password values never enter CloudKit. Each Space’s separate **Sync with iCloud Keychain** switch controls its encrypted Crest Password items. Private Spaces and transient Quick Window or Peek state are not normal synced browsing state."},"760":{"id":"/guides/sync-across-devices-7","page_id":"/guides/sync-across-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/sync-across-devices#check-status","content":"The Sync page shows whether iCloud is available and whether Crest has pending records. Apple does not expose the Apple Account email to Crest, so confirm the account directly in System Settings if two devices do not meet."},"761":{"id":"/guides/sync-across-devices-8","page_id":"/guides/sync-across-devices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/sync-across-devices#resolve-a-conflict","content":"If Crest finds different local and cloud histories, it pauses instead of merging or overwriting silently. Choose **Use This Device** only when its copy should replace iCloud. Choose **Use iCloud** only when the cloud copy should replace this device. Read the confirmation carefully because the selected copy becomes authoritative for subsequent sync."},"762":{"id":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts","page_id":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts","type":"page","content":"Set extension keyboard shortcuts","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Use extensions"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts"},"763":{"id":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts-0","page_id":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts","content":"Assign and change keyboard shortcuts for extension commands in a Crest Space."},"764":{"id":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts-1","page_id":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts#change-a-shortcut","content":"Change a shortcut"},"765":{"id":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts-2","page_id":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts#when-a-shortcut-does-nothing","content":"When a shortcut does nothing"},"766":{"id":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts-3","page_id":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts","content":"Extensions can declare keyboard commands, such as opening their popup. Chromium keeps these shortcuts for each Space's installation, so changing one in Work does not change it in Personal."},"767":{"id":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts-4","page_id":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts#change-a-shortcut","content":"Open **Crest Settings** and select the Space in the sidebar."},"768":{"id":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts-5","page_id":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts#change-a-shortcut","content":"Select **Extensions**, then **Shortcuts…**. Chromium's extension shortcuts page opens for that Space."},"769":{"id":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts-6","page_id":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts#change-a-shortcut","content":"Find the extension's command and set, change or clear its shortcut there."},"770":{"id":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts-7","page_id":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts#when-a-shortcut-does-nothing","content":"Crest's own shortcuts come first. An extension shortcut runs only when no Crest command uses the same keys. Check **Crest Settings → Shortcuts** for a conflict, and pick different keys for one of them."},"771":{"id":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts-8","page_id":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/extension-keyboard-shortcuts#when-a-shortcut-does-nothing","content":"A shortcut that opens an extension's popup shows it beside the extension's pinned icon, or beside the control that opens the window's extension list when the extension is not pinned."},"772":{"id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions","page_id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions","type":"page","content":"Manage permissions and website access per Space","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Use extensions"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions"},"773":{"id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions-0","page_id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions","content":"Review and change an extension's permissions and site access without changing another Crest Space."},"774":{"id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions-1","page_id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions#at-installation","content":"At installation"},"775":{"id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions-2","page_id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions#review-access-later","content":"Review access later"},"776":{"id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions-3","page_id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions#change-website-access","content":"Change website access"},"777":{"id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions-4","page_id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions#turn-an-extension-off-without-removing-it","content":"Turn an extension off without removing it"},"778":{"id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions-5","page_id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions#remove-it-and-its-data","content":"Remove it and its data"},"779":{"id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions-6","page_id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions","content":"Every Space keeps its own extension installations, permissions and website access. Allowing a tool in Work does not grant it the same access in Personal or on another Mac."},"780":{"id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions-7","page_id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions#at-installation","content":"The install review lists the permission warnings Chromium reports for the extension. Where the extension allows it, turn on **Withhold website access until I grant it** so the extension reaches a site only after you allow it. See Install from the Chrome Web Store."},"781":{"id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions-8","page_id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions#review-access-later","content":"Open **Crest Settings** and select the Space in the sidebar."},"782":{"id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions-9","page_id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions#review-access-later","content":"Select **Extensions**."},"783":{"id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions-10","page_id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions#review-access-later","content":"Expand the extension's row to see its **Permissions and Website Access**."},"784":{"id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions-11","page_id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions#change-website-access","content":"In the expanded row, select **Manage Permissions in Chromium**. Chromium's page for that extension opens in the same Space, where you can change its site access and other permissions. The change applies only to this Space's installation."},"785":{"id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions-12","page_id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions#turn-an-extension-off-without-removing-it","content":"Use the **Enabled** switch on the extension's row. The installation and its data in the Space stay put, ready for when you turn it back on."},"786":{"id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions-13","page_id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions#remove-it-and-its-data","content":"Expand the row, select **Remove Extension**, and confirm **Remove from _Space_**. Crest removes the extension and its data from that Space. Other Spaces are unchanged."},"787":{"id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions-14","page_id":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/manage-extension-permissions#remove-it-and-its-data","content":"Private Spaces must be unlocked before Crest shows or changes their installed extensions."},"788":{"id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups","page_id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups","type":"page","content":"Pin extensions and use extension popups","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Use extensions"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups"},"789":{"id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups-0","page_id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups","content":"Pin extension actions and use popups, side panels, and settings pages in the right Space on Mac."},"790":{"id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups-1","page_id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups#open-an-extension-action","content":"Open an extension action"},"791":{"id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups-2","page_id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups#pin-an-action","content":"Pin an action"},"792":{"id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups-3","page_id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups#open-an-extensions-settings","content":"Open an extension's settings"},"793":{"id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups-4","page_id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups#use-side-panels","content":"Use side panels"},"794":{"id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups-5","page_id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups","content":"Extension actions belong to the Space. Pin the ones you use often and leave occasional tools in Site Controls."},"795":{"id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups-6","page_id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups#open-an-extension-action","content":"Select **Site Controls** beside the address field."},"796":{"id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups-7","page_id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups#open-an-extension-action","content":"Find the extension's icon in the extension action area."},"797":{"id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups-8","page_id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups#open-an-extension-action","content":"Select the icon to run its action or open its popup."},"798":{"id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups-9","page_id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups#open-an-extension-action","content":"A popup opens below the icon you selected, attached to the Crest window. It closes when you click outside it, press Escape, move or resize the window, or switch to another app."},"799":{"id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups-10","page_id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups#open-an-extension-action","content":"Open the icon's menu for more choices: **Extension Settings…**, **Pin to Toolbar**, **Disable Extension**, **Manage Extension…**, **View on Chrome Web Store** and **Remove Extension…**. In a private window the menu offers only the choices that don't change the Space's installation."},"800":{"id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups-11","page_id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups#pin-an-action","content":"Select the pin button beside the action in Site Controls, or choose **Pin to Toolbar** from its menu. Pinned icons appear in the Space's own strip below the address field. They stay there on the Start Page too, before you open any page in the Space."},"801":{"id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups-12","page_id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups#pin-an-action","content":"To remove an icon from the strip, choose **Unpin from Toolbar**. Unpinning does not disable or uninstall the extension."},"802":{"id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups-13","page_id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups#open-an-extensions-settings","content":"If the extension has a settings page, choose **Extension Settings…** from its menu, or expand it on the Space's Extensions page in **Crest Settings** and select **Extension Settings**. The page opens in the Space that owns the installation."},"803":{"id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups-14","page_id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups#use-side-panels","content":"Extensions with a Chrome side panel open it as a card beside the page. Choose **Open Side Panel** from the action's menu, select the icon if the extension opens its panel that way, or let the extension open it itself. The panel belongs to the page it opened beside. Crest does not keep side panels after you quit."},"804":{"id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups-15","page_id":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides/pin-extensions-and-popups#use-side-panels","content":"Pinning is independent per Space and per device. A Work strip can hold work tools while Personal or another Mac uses a different set."},"805":{"id":"/guides","page_id":"/guides","type":"page","content":"Crest Help","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/guides"},"806":{"id":"/guides-0","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides","content":"Help articles for Crest on Mac, iPad, and iPhone."},"807":{"id":"/guides-1","page_id":"/guides","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides#crest-on-each-device","content":"Crest on each device"},"808":{"id":"/guides-2","page_id":"/guides","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides#get-started","content":"Get started"},"809":{"id":"/guides-3","page_id":"/guides","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides#spaces--organization","content":"Spaces & organization"},"810":{"id":"/guides-4","page_id":"/guides","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides#browse-faster","content":"Browse faster"},"811":{"id":"/guides-5","page_id":"/guides","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides#privacy-data--recovery","content":"Privacy, data & recovery"},"812":{"id":"/guides-6","page_id":"/guides","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides#install-extensions","content":"Install extensions"},"813":{"id":"/guides-7","page_id":"/guides","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides#use-extensions","content":"Use extensions"},"814":{"id":"/guides-8","page_id":"/guides","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/guides#compatibility--troubleshooting","content":"Compatibility & troubleshooting"},"815":{"id":"/guides-9","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides","content":"Crest is a browser made of Spaces. It gives work, home, research, and private browsing separate places to live, and switching Spaces changes the browsing context, not just the color of the window. Each Space keeps its own signed-in sessions, cookies, history, tabs, pinned sites, passwords, permissions, website data, appearance, and sync identity."},"816":{"id":"/guides-10","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides","content":"Crest brings Chromium and WebKit together on Mac. Read the engine and upgrade guide for website sign-ins, extensions, and choosing an engine. iPhone and iPad continue to use WebKit."},"817":{"id":"/guides-11","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides#crest-on-each-device","content":"The same Spaces and browsing model carry across Mac, iPad, and iPhone, while the controls adapt to the screen."},"818":{"id":"/guides-12","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides#crest-on-each-device","content":"| Device | How Crest fits                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Mac    | Chromium and WebKit in one app, the sidebar, Split View with two to four tabs, keyboard-first commands, Quick Window, Peek, extensions, and multiple windows. Signed, notarized releases come directly from GitHub. |","table":"table-0"},"819":{"id":"/guides-13","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides#crest-on-each-device","content":"| Device | How Crest fits                                                                                                  |\n| ------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| iPad   | The full Space structure, resizable Split View columns, touch navigation, hardware-keyboard commands, and Peek. |","table":"table-0"},"820":{"id":"/guides-14","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides#crest-on-each-device","content":"| Device | How Crest fits                                                                                                      |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| iPhone | The web page stays primary. The full sidebar becomes its own view, and Split View becomes a pager of focused cards. |","table":"table-0"},"821":{"id":"/guides-15","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides#get-started","content":"Download Crest directly, install it in Applications, and understand automatic updates."},"822":{"id":"/guides-16","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides#get-started","content":"Review imports from Arc, Zen, Chrome, Safari, Firefox, and other Chromium browsers, and export portable Crest data."},"823":{"id":"/guides-17","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides#get-started","content":"Find every major Crest setting and understand whether it applies globally or to one Space."},"824":{"id":"/guides-18","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides#get-started","content":"Choose the engine new pages open in, send a website to the other engine, and see what each engine supports."},"825":{"id":"/guides-19","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides#spaces--organization","content":"Understand how each Crest Space separates accounts, history, passwords, permissions, and website data."},"826":{"id":"/guides-20","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides#spaces--organization","content":"Design a crest, choose Space and folder colors, and configure cleanup."},"827":{"id":"/guides-21","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides#spaces--organization","content":"Use current tabs, pinned sites, saved locations, folders, Archive, and Keep Loaded deliberately."},"828":{"id":"/guides-22","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides#spaces--organization","content":"Create, focus, resize, reorder, synchronize, and separate two to four live tabs."},"829":{"id":"/guides-23","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides#spaces--organization","content":"Understand Private Space storage, history, sync, authentication, and relocking."},"830":{"id":"/guides-24","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides#spaces--organization","content":"Use iCloud to synchronize durable Spaces and resolve a device-versus-cloud conflict safely."},"831":{"id":"/guides-25","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides#spaces--organization","content":"Control Crest-owned password suggestions, generation, and save prompts independently for every Space."},"832":{"id":"/guides-26","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides#browse-faster","content":"Search, navigate, switch tabs, revisit history, and run Crest commands from one field."},"833":{"id":"/guides-27","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides#browse-faster","content":"Reference every default Crest browser shortcut and customize the complete Mac command map."},"834":{"id":"/guides-28","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides#browse-faster","content":"Learn Crest’s swipes, drags, middle-click actions, context menus, and other less-obvious interactions."},"835":{"id":"/guides-29","page_id":"/guides","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/guides#browse-faster","content":"Preview links witho