"788":595,"789":593,"790":564,"791":592,"792":565,"793":817,"794":377,"795":692,"796":399,"797":696,"798":152,"799":574,"800":697,"801":766,"802":434,"803":393,"804":599,"805":305,"806":415,"807":312,"808":414,"809":713,"810":204,"811":608,"812":457,"813":812,"814":265,"815":308,"816":286,"817":758,"818":110,"819":112,"820":111,"821":343,"822":645,"823":397,"824":238,"825":794,"826":338,"827":811,"828":285,"829":796,"830":814,"831":278,"832":671,"833":625,"834":483,"835":603,"836":211,"837":773,"838":605,"839":276,"840":674,"841":256,"842":162,"843":296,"844":298,"845":643,"846":594,"847":188,"848":680,"849":423,"850":850,"851":848,"852":720,"853":460,"854":426},"orderedDocs":[[346,"**1Password** accepts a browser you add through its **Add Browser** setting, and checks that browser's signature. See Set up 1Password in Crest."],[534,"**About** shows Crest’s build information and links to the community. On Mac, it also holds software updates: automatic checks and installs, the update channel, and **Check for Updates…**."],[511,"**Add Provider…** adds your own search engine, AI assistant or website with a name, shortcuts, search URL and color. **Restore Defaults…** puts the built-in providers' shortcuts and options back; providers you added stay."],[507,"**Also show**: **Settings Pages**, **@ Filters** such as `@tabs`, the **Calculator** and, on Mac, **Paste and Go**, which offers the address you copied when the palette opens."],[523,"**Appearance**: Crest Studio for the Space's crest, colors, and sidebar background."],[213,"**Automatically Translate** is off by default. When enabled, Crest uses your preferred device language and languages already downloaded. Showing the original keeps that page untranslated until you navigate or reload."],[662,"**Banner** uses Crest Studio: begin with a template, then choose a shape, field division, pattern, trim, and heraldic artwork. Use independent colors for the parts of your design, or make an identity with an emoji, monogram, or searchable SF Symbol."],[524,"**Browsing**: **Search with** and **Search suggestions**, which follow your default search until you choose for the Space, archiving old tabs with **Archive current tabs** and **Archive Now**, downloads (whether to ask where to save, and the download folder), and **Delete Space**."],[581,"**Clear Cache** removes only the responses Crest kept to load the site faster."],[580,"**Clear Cookies** removes the site's cookies and everything else it stored in the Space: local storage, IndexedDB, Cache Storage and service workers, including what sites embedded in it stored there. It signs you out of the site."],[228,"**Command-R** performs a normal reload. **Shift-Command-R** reloads from the origin when a cached response is not what you need. **Command-.** stops the current load."],[177,"**Contains** is useful for a domain or stable path fragment, but a pattern that is too broad may catch unrelated links."],[221,"**Copy Page Link as Markdown** uses **Option-Shift-Command-C** and produces a title-and-URL link suitable for notes or issue trackers."],[220,"**Copy Page Link** uses **Shift-Command-C**."],[666,"**Crest:** Field, Second field, Band, Emblem, Border and Edge. A color for a part the crest doesn’t draw is dimmed."],[503,"**Default search**: the search engine or AI assistant every Space uses unless it chose its own, the one **Private windows** use, and whether the default gives **Search suggestions**. **Tab to search providers** lets Tab choose a provider by its name or shortcut in the command palette, and **Space to search providers** lets a space after `$` and a shortcut, or after a shortcut alone, choose it."],[455,"**Development** follows the latest signed public `main` build and can change several times a day."],[67,"**Escape** leaves a provider or scope, then rejects a completion, then closes the palette."],[176,"**Exact** is best for one complete address that should always land in one Space."],[224,"**Export as PDF** writes a portable rendered document."],[527,"**Extensions**: available when Chromium is. **Open Chrome Web Store**, **Chromium Extension Manager**, **Shortcuts…**, and the extensions installed in the Space."],[226,"**File → Open File…** offers the archive format of the focused page's engine. Chromium cannot open a `.webarchive`, and WebKit cannot open an `.mhtml` file."],[216,"**Find in Page** uses **Command-F**. Step through matches and close Find when finished. On a Chromium page, Find shows how many matches there are and which one is selected; on a WebKit page, it shows whether there is a match."],[412,"**For a whole website:** open Site Controls and change **Opens in**. The page reloads in that engine, and later pages from the website open there too."],[411,"**For one page:** choose **Page → Open Page in WebKit** or **Open Page in Chromium**. The page reloads in the other engine. Other pages from the site keep opening where they did."],[313,"**From Chrome Web Store** for store installations;"],[347,"**iCloud Passwords** uses Apple's password helper, which Apple protects with a launch constraint on the browser's identity and entitlements. See iCloud Passwords in Crest."],[700,"**Keep Loaded** protects an important live page from ordinary unloading. It is useful for an unsaved editor, a live call, or a dashboard whose in-page state matters. Crest can still respond to genuine system memory pressure."],[454,"**Nightly** receives newer builds sooner and can change more frequently."],[647,"**Offer a copy to Passwords**, which lets the system Passwords app ask separately for a copy after Crest saves in the Space."],[526,"**Passwords**: **Use Crest Passwords**, **Sync with iCloud Keychain**, and the Space's saved passwords, with **Import Passwords…** and **Export Passwords…**."],[223,"**Print Page** uses **Command-P**."],[525,"**Privacy**: **Require Touch ID or password**, how long to keep History, Archived Tabs, and Download Records, content blocking, and saved site permissions."],[215,"**Reader** converts a supported article into a focused reading surface. Use the page controls, menu, command palette, or assign a shortcut. Reader works on WebKit pages. On Mac, open a Chromium page in WebKit to read it in Reader."],[749,"**Remove Tab From Split** takes the focused tab out of the group. **Separate All Tabs** turns every card back into an independent tab; its default shortcut is **Option-Command-U**. Closing the focused card closes that tab while the remaining group survives."],[505,"**Results**: show results under a header for each kind or **Blended** into one list, lead with a **Top Hit**, prefer an open tab over history for the same site, and **Show match reasons**, which notes under each result why it is there, such as \"Often visited\"."],[65,"**Return** runs the selected result. Hold **Command** to open it in a background tab, **Shift-Command** for a new tab, **Shift** for Split View, or **Option** for a Quick Window; the selected row shows where it will open while you hold the keys."],[225,"**Save Web Archive** saves the whole page in one file. A Chromium page saves an `.mhtml` file, and a WebKit page saves a `.webarchive` file."],[510,"**Search Engines**, **AI Assistants** and **Websites**: every provider Crest offers, each with its main shortcut. Turn a provider off to stop its shortcut; the default stays on. Click a provider to open it and see its options, such as Google's **Hide AI Overviews** or ChatGPT's **Model**, and to change its shortcuts."],[506,"**Sections**: turn each kind of result on or off, choose how many results each shows, and drag them into the order you want; **Reset Order** puts them back. Before you type, **Recent Tabs** and **Actions** show in this order."],[22,"**Settings > Agents** lists the agents connected now, with what each did lately, such as the tabs it opened and closed. Choose **Disconnect** to end one's connection."],[222,"**Share Page** opens the platform share sheet when available."],[66,"**Shift-Delete** on a history result removes it from history, and on a result the palette learned, forgets it."],[667,"**Sidebar:** Background, Accent (selected tabs, pins, the address field and the Space picker) and Pattern."],[453,"**Stable** is the normal public release cadence."],[646,"**Sync with iCloud Keychain**, which updates whether existing and future Crest credentials in that Space synchronize through the system Keychain."],[64,"**Tab** chooses the provider whose shortcut you typed, accepts a completion, or moves to the next result. **Shift-Tab** moves back."],[663,"**Traditional Gradient** keeps the familiar Arc-style theme: it blends one to three colors with direction, intensity, a readability fade, and optional texture."],[508,"**Typing**: complete addresses inline and learn from the results you choose. **Clear Learned Choices** forgets what the palette learned. Learned choices stay on this device."],[63,"**Up** and **Down** arrows, or **Control-N** and **Control-P**, move the selection; **Option-Up** and **Option-Down** jump between sections."],[217,"**Zoom In**, **Zoom Out**, and **Actual Size** use **Command-+**, **Command--**, and **Command-0**."],[41,"`delete_history` removes every visit to one `url`, without its fragment, from one allowed, unlocked `space`, once the person agrees. An address with no visits removes nothing and asks nothing."],[42,"`list_search_providers` lists the enabled search providers and a Space's default."],[38,"`list_spaces` says which Space is active and includes each unlocked Space's artwork. `list_tabs` says whether each tab is pinned or saved and which folders hold it."],[43,"`open_window`, `open_blank_window` and `open_quick_window` open a window over an allowed, unlocked Space, at an `http` or `https` address where they take one. `open_private_window` answers only with the window's ID; an address opens only in a new Private Window."],[35,"`read_page_text` answers a page's readable text as Markdown, without any form field's value. `handle_dialog` answers a page's alert, confirm or prompt, but never a question about leaving the page. `wait_for` also takes `url`, to wait until the tab's address contains it. Tools that open a window wait while Crest asks the person."],[40,"`search_history` searches the history of the allowed, unlocked Spaces, newest first. Every word of `query` must appear in the title or address, `domain` matches a host and its subdomains, and `limit` takes 1 through 1000, 25 by default."],[39,"`show_tab` shows the tab itself, opening a normal window over its Space only when none is open. `close_tab` closes only open tabs."],[159,"| Action                               | Default         |\n| ------------------------------------ | --------------- |\n| Show or Hide Developer Toolbar (Mac) | Shift-Command-I |"],[142,"| Action                           | Default         |\n| -------------------------------- | --------------- |\n| Show or Hide Translation Toolbar | Shift-Command-L |"],[113,"| Action                          | Default   |\n| ------------------------------- | --------- |\n| Open Location / command palette | Command-L |"],[111,"| Action                      | Default   |\n| --------------------------- | --------- |\n| Close Current Tab or Window | Command-W |"],[149,"| Action                     | Default                |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| Copy Page Link as Markdown | Option-Shift-Command-C |"],[135,"| Action                    | Default                    |\n| ------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| Focus Previous Split Card | Control-Command-Left Arrow |"],[128,"| Action                   | Default           |\n| ------------------------ | ----------------- |\n| Most Recent Tab Backward | Control-Shift-Tab |"],[120,"| Action                   | Default   |\n| ------------------------ | --------- |\n| Pin or Unpin Current Tab | Command-D |"],[143,"| Action                  | Default    |\n| -----------------