Where                         | Extensions |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------- |\n| WebKit pages in Crest for Mac | None       |"],[263,"| Where                    | Extensions |\n| ------------------------ | ---------- |\n| Crest on iPhone and iPad | None       |"],[376,"1Password browser code-signature requirements"],[360,"1Password checks the browser's code signature. Use the Developer ID signed and notarized Crest release installed in `/Applications`. A development build carries a different signature, and 1Password rejects it."],[373,"1Password warns that an additional browser can reach your saved information while 1Password is unlocked, so it can save and fill logins. Only authorize a Crest build you trust."],[716,"A Crest Space is not only a group of tabs. It is a separate browsing profile with its own durable organization, runtime, and privacy boundary."],[298,"A locked Space cannot receive an extension until you unlock it."],[558,"A locked Space, or one that has been deleted, cannot receive an extension or a copy."],[744,"A one-card placeholder lets you add the next tab without losing the first page."],[20,"A pointer in the agent's colour shows where it clicks, hovers, fills and scrolls."],[798,"A popup opens below the icon you selected, attached to the Crest window. It closes when you click outside it, press Escape, move or resize the window, or switch to another app."],[180,"A route targeting a protected Private Space is hidden until that Space is unlocked. This prevents its URL patterns and destination identity from leaking through Settings."],[690,"A saved tab belongs to the durable sidebar, optionally inside a folder. Its saved location is a home URL: you can navigate away, then double-click the saved-location indicator or use the context menu to return home. The context menu can replace or reset that saved location."],[771,"A shortcut that opens an extension's popup shows it beside the extension's pinned icon, or beside the control that opens the window's extension list when the extension is not pinned."],[515,"A Space's crest, colors, and sidebar background live on the Space's Appearance page. See Spaces and Customize and arrange Spaces."],[413,"A tab whose page runs in the engine that is not your default shows that engine's mark on its icon."],[696,"A tab's icon normally follows the current website. From the tab's context menu, choose **Pull New Icon** to keep the website's current icon, **Change Icon…** to choose an emoji, or **Clear Icon** to return to the automatic website icon."],[300,"A window an extension opens appears as a Crest window in the extension's Space. A requested window state, such as maximized, is ignored."],[496,"About"],[537,"Add a Chrome extension from its store page to the current Crest Space."],[842,"Add a Chrome extension from its store page to the current Crest Space."],[658,"Add and arrange Spaces"],[704,"Add device authentication"],[493,"Add, arrange, and remove Spaces"],[495,"Advanced"],[465,"After import"],[401,"After updating from a WebKit-only Crest"],[494,"Agents"],[10,"Agents are off until you turn them on."],[4,"Allow an agent"],[610,"Allow the site in Crest and allow Crest in macOS notification settings to receive notifications. On Mac, **Settings → Privacy → System permissions** shows whether macOS allows it. Document notifications belong to their open page. Chromium also supports local service-worker and extension notifications while Crest runs, including a service worker's notification after its tab closes. Private profiles do not deliver these background notifications. Locking a Space or revoking its site permission withdraws notifications it can no longer show."],[446,"Alternatively, Crest can be installed via Homebrew:"],[282,"An extension that is still enabled but whose files are gone shows no toolbar tile or settings row, and its action reports that it is unavailable."],[309,"An extension whose files are gone"],[688,"An ordinary page appears in the current-tabs area. Close or archive it when finished, or let the Space’s cleanup policy move old unpinned tabs into Archive."],[626,"An unsafe-file warning requires its own decision. Resuming a transfer does not approve a warning or bypass a block. See Malicious sites and downloads for the limits of Chromium's Google-free protection."],[32,"Any program that runs as you on your Mac can run an agent you allowed. Crest's question tells agents apart so you can see and control them; it is not a defense against harmful software already on your Mac. Allow only agents you trust, and turn agents off when you don't need them."],[486,"Appearance"],[330,"Apple protects its helper with a launch constraint on the browser. The browser must carry the managed **Web Browser Public Key Credential Requests** capability, or use an identity Apple has approved. The entitlement is:"],[329,"Apple registers its helper for Google Chrome. Crest checks Chrome's native-messaging folders when Chromium's own lookup finds nothing, so the extension can reach it. Chromium still checks that the helper allows this extension. Crest does not read your passwords; Apple's helper controls authentication and access to them."],[281,"Apple's iCloud Passwords helper checks the browser's signature and entitlements before it pairs. See iCloud Passwords in Crest."],[617,"Archive"],[622,"Archive contains manually closed or archived tabs, automatic Space cleanup, and expired Quick Windows. Filter by reason when you know how the item left the sidebar. Restoring an archived tab returns it to an appropriate live position in that Space."],[253,"Archived Quick Windows remain distinguishable in Archive so you can recover something you dismissed too quickly."],[57,"As you type the start of a site you've typed or opened before, or one a tab shows, the palette fills in the rest of its address in gray. It completes the site name, without `www.`, and once you type a `/`, the next part of the path. **Return** opens what the field shows