ng** to return to Welcome and go through setup again. Completing setup opens Getting Started in your first Space, reusing its existing guide when available."],[23,"Choose **Stop All Agents** in the Crest menu, or in **Settings > Agents**, to disconnect every agent and keep agents out of the tabs they used until Crest quits."],[21,"Choose **Stop** in that bar, or **Stop Agent in This Tab** from the badge, to keep the agent out of that tab, through any of its connections, until Crest quits or you forget the agent."],[701,"Choose **Unload** when you want to release a page but retain its tab. On Mac, middle-clicking a current tab closes it; middle-clicking a pinned or saved item unloads its page while keeping the durable item."],[189,"Choose a phone or desktop preset, or enter a custom size, in the developer toolbar. The live page renders within that viewport so you can review responsive layouts without resizing your whole browser window. Return to the normal viewport when finished."],[671,"Choose an app icon palette here too. These controls change the browser on this device; a Space’s identity belongs to that Space and stays on its own Appearance page."],[655,"Choose an identity"],[669,"Choose folder color intensity and text color on the Space’s Appearance page. Individual folder menus let you set colors, search the full SF Symbols catalog, or choose emoji. You can show a custom icon on its own instead of the animated folder artwork. In **Settings → Appearance**, enable **Tint Folder Title** to use semibold titles in the folder’s color, adjusted for stronger contrast against light or dark sidebars."],[467,"Choose one or more detected browsers, then review each source Space, profile, or window. Depending on what that browser exposes, Crest can bring across Spaces or profiles, tabs, bookmarks, saved folders, split views, tab groups, colors, icons, extensions, and supported passwords."],[397,"Choose the default engine"],[174,"Choose the destination Space."],[395,"Choose t