eate, focus, resize, reorder, synchronize, and separate two to four live tabs."],[816,"Crest brings Chromium and WebKit together on Mac. Read the engine and upgrade guide for website sign-ins, extensions, and choosing an engine. iPhone and iPad continue to use WebKit."],[599,"Crest can remember decisions for:"],[458,"Crest checks pages for unsaved work before an update restart. Choose **Stay on Page** to keep working, then retry the restart when ready. Updates are offered only when your Mac meets the whole app's macOS requirement."],[628,"Crest checks retention when it opens, after sync, and every 15 minutes while active. Shortening a duration can permanently remove older synchronized records, so Crest confirms the destructive change first."],[582,"Crest clears the whole site, such as `example.com` and its subdomains, in both engines, reloads the page, and shows the result at the top of the window. The same actions are in the command palette as **Clear Cookies for This Site** and **Clear Cache for This Site**, and on iPhone and iPad in the page menu. In a private window, they clear only what that window holds in memory."],[349,"Crest does not copy Chrome's profile or read a companion app's data."],[563,"Crest does not install Firefox add-ons from **addons.mozilla.org**."],[559,"Crest does not install Firefox add-ons or Safari Web Extensions. Look for the extension's Chrome version."],[264,"Crest does not install Firefox add-ons or Safari Web Extensions. Many of them also publish a Chrome version. See Firefox add-ons and Safari Web Extensions."],[562,"Crest does not install Firefox add-ons. Use an extension's Chrome Web Store version instead."],[843,"Crest does not install Firefox add-ons. Use an extension's Chrome Web Store version instead."],[568,"Crest does not scan Mac apps for Safari Web Extensions. Use an extension's Chrome Web Store version instead."],[844,"Crest does not scan Mac apps for Safari Web Extensions. Use an extension's Chrome Web Store version instead."],[569,"Crest does not scan the apps on your Mac for Safari Web Extensions, and it cannot add one from an app bundle."],[299,"Crest does not yet match Chrome for every extension API. A feature that needs part of Chrome's window that Crest does not draw may be missing."],[404,"Crest for Mac includes two web engines. New pages open in Chromium unless you choose otherwise, and any website or page can use WebKit, the engine behind Safari. Crest on iPhone and iPad uses WebKit."],[543,"Crest for Mac installs Chrome extensions from the Chrome Web Store. Extensions run on Chromium pages. Pages you open in WebKit, and Crest on iPhone and iPad, run no extensions."],[441,"Crest for Mac requires Apple silicon and macOS 26.1 or later. It is distributed directly as a signed and notarized app with Chromium and WebKit; see Chromium and WebKit on Mac. Crest for iPhone and iPad is on the App Store and continues to use WebKit."],[291,"Crest for Mac runs Chrome extensions from the Chrome Web Store on its Chromium engine. The extension compatibility page lists which browser features Crest connects to its interface. This page collects the limits."],[805,"Crest Help"],[33,"Crest includes a Model Context Protocol server as a helper inside the app, which an agent runs over its standard input and output:"],[594,"Crest includes a small built-in ad and tracker ruleset that can be enabled or disabled per Space. It uses WebKit, so it applies on iPhone, iPad, and WebKit pages on Mac. Use the site controls or assign **Toggle Content Blocking** a shortcut when a site needs a quick exception."],[815,"Crest is a browser made of Spaces. It gives work, home, research, and private browsing separate places to live, and switching Spaces changes the browsing context, not just the color of the window. Each Space keeps its own signed-in sessions, cookies, history, tabs, pinned sites, passwords, permissions, website data, appearance, and sync identity."],[15,"Crest must be open while an agent works. Before an agent opens a window, Crest asks you; you can let it open windows without asking until it disconnects, except private windows, which Crest always asks about."],[59,"Crest offers search engines such as Google, DuckDuckGo, Bing, Brave Search and Startpage; AI assistants such as ChatGPT, Claude and Perplexity; and websites such as YouTube, Wikipedia, GitHub, Reddit and Amazon. Turn providers on or off, change their shortcuts, set their options, choose your default search and the one private windows use, and add your own in **Settings → Search**. Search providers stay on this device."],[661,"Crest offers two presentation styles:"],[807,"Crest on each device"],[721,"Crest Passwords and optional iCloud Keychain participation"],[635,"Crest Passwords are private to the Space that owns them. You can stop using Crest-owned suggestions, generation, and save prompts in one Space without deleting its saved passwords or changing another Space."],[651,"Crest Passwords are saved in the system Keychain and suggested only for matching websites. Viewing, copying, or exporting a password can require device authentication."],[430,"Crest Passwords handles saved passwords. Built-in address and payment-card autofill are not available."],[310,"Crest shows each extension's basic state in its own settings. Chromium's extension manager holds the detailed record: errors, permissions and site access."],[393,"Crest shows popups, side panels, extension windows and keyboard shortcuts in its own interface. An extension that expects part of Chrome's window that Crest does not draw may lose that feature. See Extension compatibility."],[665,"Crest Studio is on the Space’s Appearance page. The crest sits on the Space’s own sidebar background, with its colors named by what they paint:"],[758,"Crest synchronizes durable browser structure such as Spaces, tabs, saved folders, Split View groups, appearance, Archive, history, and supported preferences. Mac, iPad, and iPhone then render the same model in