ge formats"],[257,"Packages"],[208,"Page actions operate on the focused page. In Split View, click or tap a card first so the intended page owns the command."],[100,"Page tools"],[382,"Password managers and companion apps"],[759,"Password values never enter CloudKit. Each Space’s separate **Sync with iCloud Keychain** switch controls its encrypted Crest Password items. Private Spaces and transient Quick Window or Peek state are not normal synced browsing state."],[232,"Peek"],[238,"Peek and Quick Window are transient browsing surfaces. Both use a real Crest Space profile so the page can access the right signed-in session and Crest Passwords, but neither has to become a durable tab."],[239,"Peek opens a link above the source page. Close it to return immediately, or choose **Open In…** to promote it into a full tab in the current Space or another one. **Command-W** closes an open Peek and **Command-O** promotes it."],[241,"Peek stays attached to its source tab when you open another tab or switch Spaces. Return to the source tab to continue in its Peek. If the source is one card in Split View, promotion and page commands follow that focused card."],[791,"Pin an action"],[789,"Pin extension actions and use popups, side panels, and settings pages in the right Space on Mac."],[846,"Pin extension actions and use popups, side panels, and settings pages in the right Space on Mac."],[788,"Pin extensions and use extension popups"],[679,"Pinned sites"],[689,"Pinned sites appear as a compact icon grid near the top of a Space. Use them for always-close destinations such as mail, calendar, or a dashboard. Choose **Pin or Unpin Current Tab** or press **Command-D**. You can also right-click a tab and choose **Pin Tab**, or right-click a pinned tab and choose **Unpin Tab**; on iPhone and iPad, touch and hold the tab instead."],[675,"Pinned sites, saved tabs, folders, and tabs marked **Keep Loaded** have different roles from ordinary current tabs. Use a saved tab for something you int