llows a Top Hit."],[17,"The first time an agent uses Crest, Crest asks whether to allow it. The question names the program macOS verified by its code signature, not the name the agent gives itself. Crest remembers your answer and lists the agent under **Allowed agents**. Choose **Forget** to disconnect it; Crest asks again the next time it connects."],[328,"The iCloud Passwords extension installs from the Chrome Web Store into Crest for Mac and runs on Chromium pages. It is only half of iCloud Passwords. The other half is Apple's system password helper, which the extension reaches through native messaging."],[780,"The install review lists the permission warnings Chromium reports for the extension. Where the extension allows it, turn on **Withhold website access until I grant it** so the extension reaches a site only after you allow it. See Install from the Chrome Web Store."],[319,"The manager shows what Chrome's does, including errors the extension reported. Include them, with the extension version, Crest version and the steps that fail, in a bug report."],[68,"The palette learns which result you choose for what you type, so the result you usually pick for \"gi\" leads next time. It remembers this for each Space on this device only, never syncs it, and never learns in a private window. Clearing a Space's history forgets it too, and **Settings → Search → Clear Learned Choices** forgets everything it learned."],[420,"The previous stable 0.6 release used WebKit only. Updating to Crest 0.7 keeps your Spaces, tabs, history and Crest Passwords. New pages open in Chromium unless you choose WebKit as your default. Each engine keeps separate website data, so Chromium does not inherit your WebKit sign-ins. Your existing WebKit website data remains available to pages opened in WebKit."],[664,"The result appears in the Space picker and browser chrome on Mac, iPad, and iPhone."],[457,"The same installer updates older WebKit-only versions and versions that already include Chromium. Your Spaces and browser records stay in place. Chromium and WebKit keep separate website sign-ins, and older WebKit extension installations do not carry over. See Upgrading from a WebKit-only Crest before switching engines."],[645,"The same page lists the Space’s saved passwords, with **Import Passwords…** and **Export Passwords…**. When Crest Passwords is on, supported Mac builds can also show:"],[817,"The same Spaces and browsing model carry across Mac, iPad, and iPhone, while the controls adapt to the screen."],[509,"The search providers come last:"],[331,"The signed Crest release carries this entitlement. Development and review builds do not, so iCloud Passwords cannot pair in them. Adding the entitlement to a build yourself does not authorize it; Apple checks it against the app's provisioning."],[760,"The Sync page shows whether iCloud is available and whether Crest has pending records. Apple does not expose the Apple Account email to Crest, so confirm the account directly in System Settings if two devices do not meet."],[105,"These are the current defaults. On Mac, open **Settings → Shortcuts** to search the whole catalog, record a new shortcut, clear an assignment, inspect conflicts, or restore the default. Commands marked **Unassigned** remain available from the menu and command palette."],[190,"This previews the page’s layout at the chosen dimensions; it does not reproduce another device’s hardware or browser engine."],[595,"To change it for a Space, turn **Block known ads and trackers** on or off in that Space’s privacy settings. On Mac, open Settings, select the Space in the sidebar, then select **Privacy**. On iPhone and iPad, open **Settings → Privacy** and choose the Space."],[550,"To install the same package in more Spaces, select **Install in other Spaces…** and choose them."],[801,"To remove an icon from the strip, choose **Unpin from Toolbar**. Unpinning does not disable or uninstall the extension."],[16,"To start Crest without bringing it to the front, a tool can run `open -g --env CREST_BACKGROUND_LAUNCH=1 -a Crest`. Crest opens your windows behind the app you're using, and comes forward only to ask you something, such as about an agent it hasn't met."],[195,"Toggle the inspector's Console, Network panel, or element inspection."],[184,"Toolbar controls"],[81,"Touch and hold tabs, folders, links, and Space controls for context actions."],[201,"Translate a page"],[210,"Translate webpages on device using Apple’s Translation framework. Whole-page translation works on iPhone, iPad, and Mac, where it works on both Chromium and WebKit pages. On a Chromium page you can also select text and translate the selection from the page's context menu; it uses the same on-device translation."],[837,"Translate webpages on device, read without distractions, share, and export pages."],[200,"Translate webpages on device, use Reader, find text, adjust zoom, share, and export pages."],[199,"Translate, read, and use page tools"],[377,"Troubleshoot an extension"],[379,"Try these first"],[639,"Turn **Use Crest Passwords** on or off."],[643,"Turn **Use Crest Passwords** on or off."],[777,"Turn an extension off without removing it"],[451,"Turn automatic checks and installs on or off in **Settings → About**, which also has **Check for Updates…**. You can also open the app menu and choose **Check for Updates**. A manual check uses the same signed update channel as the automatic check."],[630,"Turn Crest Passwords on or off per Space"],[12,"Turn on **Allow agents to use Crest**."],[93,"Turn on **Focus follows pointer** in **Settings → Tabs** if moving the pointer between Split View cards should move focus too."],[3,"Turn on agents"],[25,"Turning agents off disconnects every agent."],[60,"Type `@tabs`, `@history`, `@saved`, `@actions`, or `@spaces` and press **Space** or **Tab** to list every match of that kind and nothing else. Leave the same way you leave a provider. Turn these off with **@ Filters** in **Settings → Search**."],[58,"Type a provider's shortcut, such as **g** for Google, **ddg** for DuckDuckGo, **yt** for YouTube, **w** for Wikipedia, or **claude**, and press **Tab**; this needs **Tab to search providers**, which is on unless you turn it off. While you type the first word, every provider it names or starts to name shows as a chip under the field, with its shortcut; the first is the one **Tab** chooses, and you can click any of them. Once a provider is chosen, a chip with its icon and color appears beside the field. Type your search and press **Return** to search that provider, or to ask an AI assistant. When what you typed is exactly a shortcut, **Tab** chooses the provider even while the field completes an address. Type `$` before a shortcut, such as `$yt`, and a space to choose the provider without pressing **Tab**. **Space to search providers** in **Settings → Search** turns this off, or lets a shortcut alone, such as `yt`, and a space choose the provider too. Its suggestions, where it offers them, come only from that provider. Press **Escape**, **Delete** in an empty field, or the chip's close control to leave and keep your text."],[61,"Type a verb or feature name such as \"archive,\" \"downloads,\" \"reader,\" \"split,\" or \"copy Markdown.\" Initials work too, such as \"tsv\" for Toggle Split View. The palette uses the same command catalog as the Mac menus and shortcut settings, so an action stays discoverable even when it has no key equivalent. Settings pages appear the same way."],[62,"Type arithmetic such as `24 * 7` to see the answer; **Return** copies it."],[14,"Under **Connect an Agent**, choose **Copy Setup** for your agent, and paste it in your agent's terminal or settings."],[13,"Under **Spaces**, turn on each Space agents may use."],[711,"Understand how each Crest Space separates accounts, history, passwords, permissions, and website data."],[825,"Understand how each Crest Space separates accounts, history, passwords, permissions, and website data."],[703,"Understand Private Space storage, history, sync, authentication, and relocking."],[829,"Understand Private Space storage, history, sync, authentication, and relocking."],[294,"Unpacked extensions install from Chromium's extension manager in developer mode."],[334,"Until it pairs, use Crest's built-in passwords for the Space or another password manager."],[438,"Update channels"],[541,"Updates"],[439,"Updating from an older Crest"],[194,"Use **Capture in Portrait Mode**, **Copy Full Page Capture**, or drag a region to copy it."],[623,"Use **Command-E** to archive the current tab, **Shift-Command-T** to reopen the last closed tab, and **Shift-Command-K** to clear unpinned current tabs into Archive."],[248,"Use **Command-N** for another window onto your shared Spaces and tabs. Each window keeps its own selected Space and tab. Organizing or closing a tab changes the shared workspace; closing the window itself keeps your tabs available in the other windows."],[197,"Use **Option-Command-I**, the menu, or the command palette; the same shortcut closes it again. A Chromium page opens Chromium DevTools in the window, and a WebKit page opens Web Inspector. The inspector follows the focused page, including the focused card inside Split View."],[250,"Use **Option-Command-N** for a **New Blank Window**: a disposable workspace using the current Space's cookies, passwords, extensions, and settings. Its tabs, folders, history, and archive are temporary, stay out of iCloud sync, and are discarded when the window closes. It shares the Space's signed-in website session; use a Private Space when you need temporary website storage too."],[452,"Use **Settings → About** to choose the update channel:"],[188,"Use **Shift-Command-I** to show or hide the toolbar on any website. To stop the toolbar opening by itself on local addresses, turn off **Developer toolbar on local pages** in **Settings > General**. The shortcut still shows it whenever you want it."],[739,"Use any of these paths:"],[677,"Use current tabs, pinned sites, saved locations, folders, Archive, and Keep Loaded deliberately."],[827,"Use current tabs, pinned sites, saved locations, folders, Archive, and Keep Loaded deliberately."],[813,"Use extensions"],[753,"Use iCloud to synchronize durable Spaces and resolve a device-versus-cloud conflict safely."],[830,"Use iCloud to synchronize durable Spaces and resolve a device-versus-cloud conflict safely."],[540,"Use it after installation"],[230,"Use Peek and Quick Window"],[793,"Use side panels"],[730,"Use Split View"],[785,"Use the **Enabled** switch on the extension's row. The installation and its data in the Space stay put, ready for when you turn it back on."],[699,"Use the archive control on the sidebar divider to clear open tabs while keeping pinned and saved tabs. Closed tabs remain recoverable in Archive, subject to the Space’s retention settings."],[44,"Use the command palette"],[86,"Use the normal two-finger Back and Forward gesture inside web content; the page's engine owns the page-navigation gesture."],[219,"Use the sidebar’s Now Playing controls for eligible active media. On Mac, supported videos can open in **Picture in Picture**. Turn on **Picture in Picture when switching tabs** in **Settings → General** to start it automatically. Availability depends on the website and its player."],[348,"Use the signed and notarized Crest release in `/Applications`. A development build carries a different signature, and companion apps that check the signature reject it."],[203,"Video and audio"],[547,"Wait while Crest downloads the package from Google's update service. Chromium checks the publisher's signature and the extension's ID before the review appears."],[335,"Web Browser Public Key Credential entitlement"],[578,"Website data belongs to the Space that stored it, and it stays on this device. Clearing it in one Space never touches another Space, your saved passwords, extensions, downloaded files, or site permissions."],[399,"Website rules"],[6,"What agents can reach"],[325,"What Apple checks"],[712,"What belongs to one Space"],[340,"What Crest does not do"],[402,"What each engine supports"],[705,"What private browsing does not do"],[754,"What sync carries"],[52,"What the palette remembers"],[247,"When a page opens a popup window, like a **Sign in with Google** or **Sign in with Apple** window, Crest for Mac shows it in a Quick Window in the same Space. The popup stays connected to the page that opened it, uses the same engine as that page, and closes itself when the sign-in finishes. Choose **Open in** and the Space to keep it as a tab instead, or close the Quick Window to drop it. A page that opens a new tab, rather than a popup window, still opens a tab beside it. On iPhone and iPad, a popup opens as a tab."],[36,"When a page runs on WebKit, input reaches it as script events, which some pages ignore, and its network requests show their address, type and timing without their method, status or headers."],[765,"When a shortcut does nothing"],[693,"When an extension groups tabs, as Claude does with the tabs it works in, the group appears as a current folder with the group's name and color. Editing that folder changes the group the extension sees. See Extension compatibility."],[644,"When Crest Passwords is off, saved passwords remain in that Space until you delete them. Turning the setting back on makes them available to matching sites again."],[18,"When the program is a general interpreter, such as node or python, allowing it covers any program it runs under the same agent name."],[249,"When two windows show the same tab, the focused window holds the live page and the other displays its preview. Focus the other window to continue there with the same page state."],[542,"When you can't install"],[256,"Where extensions run"],[285,"Where extensions run in Crest, and the limits that apply to them."],[851,"Where extensions run in Crest, and the limits that apply to them."],[255,"Which extensions Crest runs, where, and which Chrome extension features Crest connects to its own interface."],[850,"Which extensions Crest runs, where, and which Chrome extension features Crest connects to its own interface."],[97,"Windows and navigation"],[708,"You can require Touch ID, Face ID, or the device passcode before opening a protected Private Space. On Mac, turn on **Require Touch ID or password** on the Space’s Privacy page in Settings. Crest can relock protected content when the app leaves the foreground so another person cannot return to it from the app switcher."],[405,"Your Spaces, tabs, history, passwords and settings are the same whichever engine shows a page. Website data is not: each engine keeps its own cookies and storage for a Space, so signing in to a site in Chromium does not sign you in to it in WebKit."]],"type":"string"},"page_id":{"docs":{"1":62,"2":63,"3":64,"4":65,"5":66,"6":67,"7":68,"8":69,"9":70,"10":71,"11":72,"12":73,"13":74,"14":75,"15":76,"16":77,"17":78,"18":79,"19":80,"20":81,"21":82,"22":83,"23":84,"24":85,"25":86,"26":87,"27":88,"28":89,"29":90,"30":91,"31":92,"32":93,"33":94,"34":95,"35":96,"36":97,"37":98,"38":99,"39":100,"40":101,"41":102,"42":103,"43":104,"44":105,"45":106,"46":107,"47":108,"48":109,"49":110,"50":111,"51":112,"52":113,"53":114,"54":115,"55":116,"56":117,"57":118,"58":119,"59":120,"60":121,"61":122,"62":123,"63":124,"64":125,"65":126,"66":127,"67":128,"68":129,"69":130,"70":324,"71":325,"72":326,"73":327,"74":328,"75":329,"76":330,"77":331,"78":332,"79":333,"80":334,"81":335,"82":336,"83":337,"84":338,"85":339,"86":340,"87":341,"88":342,"89":343,"90":344,"91":345,"92":346,"93":347,"94":348,"95":436,"96":437,"97":438,"98":439,"99":440,"100":441,"101":442,"102":443,"103":444,"104":445,"105":446,"106":447,"107":448,"108":449,"109":450,"110":451,"111":452,"112":453,"113":454,"114":455,"115":456,"116":457,"117":458,"118":459,"119":460,"120":461,"121":462,"122":463,"123":464,"124":465,"125":466,"126":467,"127":468,"128":469,"129":470,"130":471,"1